== Trivia ==
{{Gallery}}
* Timepiece phase II is GUITARFREAKS 10thMIX & drummania 9thMIX's PREMIUM ENCORE STAGE. Timepiece phase II is accessed by earning at least 98% Perfects on [[Agnus Dei]] or [[cockpit]] on EXTRA STAGE, up to the highest difficulty tier played on EXTRA STAGE.
** It is the first PREMIUM ENCORE STAGE introduced in the GuitarFreaks & DrumMania series.
** Timepiece phase II is available in [[AC GF11DM10|GUITARFREAKS 11thMIX & drummania 10thMIX]] as an EXTRA STAGE, and can be unlocked with an [[e-amusement|e-AMUSEMENT]] account at 200 Skill Points. Timepiece phase II is immediately available in Standard Mode as of [[AC GFDM V|GuitarFreaks V & DrumMania V]].
*** This is also the first time the ENCORE STAGE of the previous game was not made immediately available in Standard Mode in the following game.
* Timepiece phase II's original GuitarFreaks & DrumMania charts were created by [[Asaki]].
* Timepiece phase II received a new banner in [[AC GFDM V|GuitarFreaks V & DrumMania V]].
* Timepiece phase II is also [[CS GFDM MPS|GuitarFreaks & DrumMania MASTERPIECE SILVER]]'s PREMIUM ENCORE STAGE. Timepiece phase II is accessed by earning at least 98% Perfects on either [[CLASSIC PARTY 3]], [[VOIDDD]], or [[One Phrase Blues]] as EXTRA STAGE, up to the highest difficulty tier played on EXTRA STAGE.
** It's also available as an unlock with time-released unlocks by playing Arcade mode for 19.5 hours.
* Timepiece phase II is Hirofumi Sasaki's final song credited to his name in the GuitarFreaks & DrumMania series.
** It's also the only song in GuitarFreaks & DrumMania credited under his name that does not feature [[Yoshihiko Koezuka]] on bass.
* Timepiece phase II is the ''GUITARFREAKS 10thMIX & drummania 9thMIX LIMIT BURST'' (EXTRA STAGE) song of beatmania IIDX 20 tricoro. It was made available to play on January 23rd, 2013.
** In [[AC SPADA|beatmania IIDX 21 SPADA]], its NORMAL, HYPER, and ANOTHER charts can be unlocked by obtaining 133, 142, and 151 Tran Medals respectively.
** As of July 24th, 2014, it could be unlocked in beatmania IIDX 21 SPADA and [[AC PENDUAL|22 PENDUAL]] through the [[Hakken! Yomigaetta BEMANI iseki|発見！よみがえったBEMANI遺跡]] event.
** As of July 1st, 2015, it could be purchased in beatmania IIDX 22 PENDUAL with ''Youkou no hologram'' (陽光のホログラム).
** As of [[AC copula|beatmania IIDX 23 copula]], it is available by default.
* An alternate set of charts for Timepiece phase II featuring Charge Notes, titled '''Timepiece phase II (CN Ver.)''', can be found in beatmania IIDX 20 tricoro.
** Even over three weeks since Timepiece phase II was added to tricoro, both sets of charts were still in LIMIT BURST Phase 3, while all other LIMIT BURST songs were in Phase 4 and can be unlocked by simply playing three songs from their corresponding series.
** In [[AC SPADA|beatmania IIDX 21 SPADA]], its NORMAL, HYPER, and ANOTHER charts can be unlocked by obtaining 134, 143, and 152 Tran Medals respectively, the most of any tricoro unlock.
* In [[AC tricoro (China)|beatmania IIDX tricoro 狂热节拍IIDX2]], the titles of Timepiece phase II and Timepiece phase II (CN ver.) are written as '''TimePiece phase II''' and '''TimePiece phase II CN-Edition''' respectively.
* The sun from Timepiece phase II's video would later become a selectable character in [[AC GD OverDrive|GITADORA OverDrive]]'s Battle System.
* Timepiece phase II was added to ノスタルジア on March 15th, 2017 as part of the ''NOSTALGIA launch memorial song crossover campaign'' (ノスタルジア稼働記念 楽曲交換キャンペーン).
* Timepiece phase II is available in [[CS INFINITAS|beatmania IIDX INFINITAS]] by purchasing '''beatmania IIDX INFINITAS Music Pack vol.3''' (beatmania IIDX INFINITAS 楽曲パック vol.3).
* Timepiece phase II (CN Ver.) is available in beatmania IIDX INFINITAS by purchasing '''beatmania IIDX INFINITAS Music Pack vol.4''' (beatmania IIDX INFINITAS 楽曲パック vol.4).
* Timepiece phase II is one of the unlocks of the ''pop'n time trip'' (ポップンタイムトリップ) event. It could be unlocked from March 11th, 2019 to February 19th, 2020 by filling out the second GITADORA 20th card.
** As of November 5th, 2020, it is available by default.
* In pop'n music, instead of displaying its character's portrait, Timepiece phase II displays its jacket on the song selection screen.
* Timepiece phase II (CLASSIC) is the ''GF&DM CHRONICLE'' 2002～2004 PREMIUM ENCORE STAGE in [[AC GD EXCHAIN|GITADORA EXCHAIN]]. It could be unlocked from April 3rd, 2019 by clearing it as a PREMIUM ENCORE STAGE, by first earning at least 98% PERFECTs on Agnus Dei (CLASSIC) or cockpit (CLASSIC) on ENCORE STAGE.
** In [[AC GD NEX+AGE|GITADORA NEX+AGE]], it could be unlocked from March 4th to June 21st, 2020 and from October 28th to November 29th, 2020 as part of the ''Thank you! GITADORA 21st kanshasai'' (サンキュー! ギタドラ21st感謝祭) event.
*** It could also be unlocked from July 8th to August 2nd, 2020 and from December 2nd, 2020 to January 3rd, 2021 as part of the ''GITADORA wo tomodachi to issho ni play shiyou!! Campaign'' (GITADORAを友達と一緒にプレーしよう!!キャンペーン).
** As of [[AC GD FUZZ-UP|GITADORA FUZZ-UP]], it is available by default.
* Timepiece phase II and its CLASSIC charts are available in [[CS GD Konasute|コナステ GITADORA]] by purchasing '''Konasute GITADORA HISTORY PACK vol.4''' (コナステ GITADORA HISTORYパック vol.4).
* In the DanceDanceRevolution and SOUND VOLTEX series, Timepiece phase II's title is shown as '''Timepiece phase Ⅱ'''.
* Timepiece phase Ⅱ is available in DanceDanceRevolution GRAND PRIX from September 19th, 2024, by purchasing '''BEMANI SELECTION music pack vol.2''' (BEMANI SELECTION楽曲パック vol.2).
** Prior to its appearance in GRAND PRIX, Timepiece phase II was listed in the DanceDanceRevolution master song list between the songs from [[AC DDR SuperNOVA|SuperNOVA]].
* Despite Timepiece phase Ⅱ's listed BPMs, its DanceDanceRevolution charts actually reach as low as 91 BPM at the very end.
** In DanceDanceRevolution GRAND PRIX, Timepiece phase Ⅱ's BPM is mistakenly shown as 31-287 regardless of the difficulty selected.
* Timepiece phase Ⅱ features a modified widescreen version of its GuitarFreaks & DrumMania video in the DanceDanceRevolution series, which eliminates any on-screen dancers in DanceDanceRevolution GRAND PRIX.
** Timepiece phase Ⅱ's DanceDanceRevolution video consists of the original GuitarFreaks & DrumMania video tiled three times across the screen.
** The GuitarFreaks & DrumMania series also use this video for its regular and CLASSIC charts as of [[AC GD GALAXY WAVE DELTA|GITADORA GALAXY WAVE DELTA]].
* Timepiece phase Ⅱ is available in SOUND VOLTEX EXCEED GEAR コナステ from September 19th, 2024, by purchasing '''Konasute SOUND VOLTEX BEMANI Selection Music Pack vol.2''' (コナステ版 SOUND VOLTEX BEMANI セレクション 楽曲パック vol.2).
* 770 is uncredited in Timepiece phase Ⅱ's jacket credits in the SOUND VOLTEX series.
* Timepiece phase Ⅱ is one of DanceDanceRevolution WORLD's ''EXTRA SAVIOR WORLD'' songs. It can be unlocked from April 10th, 2025.
* Timepiece phase Ⅱ was added to SOUND VOLTEX EXCEED GEAR on September 11th, 2025.
* Timepiece phase II received a Real chart in [[AC NST Op.3|ノスタルジア Op.3]] on October 22nd, 2026.

