* On April 13th, 2016, a link of a mysterious site titled [http://web.archive.org/web/20170623142449/https://p.eagate.573.jp/game/jubeat/qubell/p/gfs/ G.F.S.] appeared on the jubeat Qubell [[e-amusement|eAMUSEMENT]] site, with a date and a message posted on it every few days. On the April 27th, 2016 ''BEMANI Namahosou (kari)'' (BEMANI生放送(仮)) stream, the meaning of the G.F.S. site was revealed: Glitter Flatter Scatter's design page.
** The dates and messages posted on the site referred to previous Project B- songs' release dates and names.
* Glitter Flatter Scatter ranked #1 in the BEMANI Fan Site CHECK!SONGS Monthly Ranking list for May 2016.
* Glitter Flatter Scatter is part of the [[POLICY BREAK]] event. For more information on the dates it could be unlocked in the SOUND VOLTEX series, please see the event page.
** From November 15th, 2018 in SOUND VOLTEX IV HEAVENLY HAVEN, it can be purchased with BLOCKs instead.
** On September 7th, 2017, a bug occurred in which playing jubeat clan did not fill the POLICY BREAK gauge, regardless of mode played. This was fixed later the same day.
* Glitter Flatter Scatter was added to [[CS SDVX III|SOUND VOLTEX III GRAVITY WARS コナステ]]'s REGULAR course on August 1st, 2019.
** It is also available in GRAVITY WARS コナステ's INFINITE course and [[CS SDVX EG|EXCEED GEAR コナステ]] from January 8th, 2020, by purchasing '''Konasute SOUND VOLTEX Music Pack vol.7''' (コナステ版 SOUND VOLTEX 楽曲パック vol.7).
* Glitter Flatter Scatter also appears in jubeat (2021)'s plus mode, as part of the '''Qubell pack 19'''.
* Glitter Flatter Scatter is available in DanceDanceRevolution GRAND PRIX's GRAND PRIX mode from June 24th, 2022, by purchasing '''SPECIAL music pack feat.jubeat vol.2''' (スペシャル楽曲パック feat.jubeat vol.2).
** By purchasing this pack with an active subscription, Glitter Flatter Scatter could be played in DanceDanceRevolution A3.
** From June 30th, 2023 in DanceDanceRevolution A3, it is available by default for all players.
* Glitter Flatter Scatter being crossed over to the DanceDanceRevolution series marks it as the first Akhuta song to appear in a BEMANI game since his departure from KONAMI.
* Glitter Flatter Scatter's MAXIMUM chart was slightly changed in [[AC SDVX NABLA|SOUND VOLTEX ∇]].

