== Song Connections / Remixes ==
* サヨナラ・ヘヴン is the second song in 猫叉Master's CONTEMPORARY NATION song series.
* A long version of サヨナラ・ヘヴン appears in the [[pop'n music 13 Carnival AC & CS pop'n music 11|pop'n music 13 カーニバル AC ♥ CS pop'n music 11]] original soundtrack, as well as in 猫叉Master's first album, [[Raindrops]].
* REFLEC BEAT uses a shorter version of サヨナラ・ヘヴン, cutting out the beginning and ending parts of the song.
** Despite this, the [[REFLEC BEAT ORIGINAL SOUNDTRACK]] features the full, uncut version of the song.
** As of [[AC RB groovin'!!|REFLEC BEAT groovin']], サヨナラ・ヘヴン uses the uncut version of the song as well.
* A bossa nova arrangement of サヨナラ・ヘヴン by [[Daisuke Oshima|大嶋大輔]] appears in the [[pop'n music Cafe music selection]] album.
* A remix of サヨナラ・ヘヴン by [[Masaya Oya|かめりあ]], titled [[Sayonara heaven (Camellia's NEKOMATAelectroRMX)|サヨナラ・ヘヴン （かめりあ's NEKOMATAelectroRMX）]], appears in [[AC SDVX|SOUND VOLTEX BOOTH]].
* サヨナラ・ヘヴン appears as part of the ''PM SUPER BEST すぺしゃるメドレー'', a medley by [[Tsugumi Kataoka]] that appears in the [[pop'n music SUPER BEST BOX]] compilation album.
* A rock arrangement of サヨナラ・ヘヴン by [[Mutsuhiko Izumi]], titled [[Sayonara heaven -GITADOROCK ver.-|サヨナラ・ヘヴン -GITADOROCK ver.-]], appears in [[AC GD Tri-Boost|GITADORA Tri-Boost]].
* An EDM remix of サヨナラ・ヘヴン by [[Ryutaro Nakahara|Ryu☆]], titled ''サヨナラ・ヘヴン (Ryu☆Remix SLver)'', appears in Ryu☆'s third anthology album, [[Ryu BEST -SUNLiGHT-|Ryu☆BEST -SUNLiGHT-]].
* A chiptune arrangement of サヨナラ・ヘヴン by [[sinoryu|しのりゅー]], titled ''サヨナラ・ヘヴン-Celtic Chip Dance Mix-'', appears in the [[CS ULTIMATE MOBILE|beatmania IIDX ULTIMATE MOBILE]] exclusive album [[BEMANI 8bit collection]].
** A short version of サヨナラ・ヘヴン-Celtic Chip Dance Mix-, titled [[Sayonara heaven-Celtic Chip Dance Mix-|サヨナラ・ヘヴン(Celtic Chip Dance Mix)]], also appears as a playable song in beatmania IIDX ULTIMATE MOBILE.
* The ノスタルジア series uses a piano arrangement of サヨナラ・ヘヴン.
* A symphonic arrangement of サヨナラ・ヘヴン by [[Tadahiro Tsuchiya|Morrigan]] feat.Lily, titled ''サヨナラ・ヘヴン (Orchestra Arr.)'', appears in the [[BEMANI SYMPHONY ORIGINAL SOUNDTRACK]] album.
** A short version of サヨナラ・ヘヴン (Orchestra Arr.), titled [[Sayonara heaven (BEMANI SYMPHONY Arr.)|サヨナラ・ヘヴン (BEMANI SYMPHONY Arr.)]], appears in [[CS jb 2021|jubeat (2021)]].

