== Trivia ==
* 伐折羅-vajra- was unveiled in the final round of the REFLEC BEAT groovin'!! Upper section of [[KONAMI Arcade Championship|The 4th KONAMI Arcade Championship]] event.
* 伐折羅-vajra- marks Yoshihiro Tagawa's first collaboration of aliases.
* Vajra is a Sanskrit word meaning both thunderbolt and diamond. It is the name of a weapon that is used as a ritual object to symbolize both the properties of a diamond (indestructibility) and a thunderbolt (irresistible force).
* 伐折羅-vajra- was added to REFLEC BEAT groovin'!! Upper on February 16th, 2015 to the winners of the ''REFLEC derby'' (リフレクダービー) event, which started on January 30th, 2015, and ended on February 14th, 2015.
** It could be unlocked by all players from August 20th, 2015 to September 3rd, 2015 as part of the ''Kagayake! vajra michi'' (耀け！伐折羅道) event.
** In [[AC RB VOLZZA|REFLEC BEAT VOLZZA]], 伐折羅-vajra-'s BASIC, MEDIUM, and HARD charts could be purchased in the Garage for 20, 30, and 40 VOLZZA KEYs, respectively.
** In [[AC RB VOLZZA 2|REFLEC BEAT VOLZZA 2]], 伐折羅-vajra- was playable by default.
* Prior to its revival in [[AC RB Reflesia|REFLEC BEAT 悠久のリフレシア]], 伐折羅-vajra-'s charts have notecounts that are multiples of 333.
** Also, its BASIC and MEDIUM charts are the second and third charts to be rated Level 6 and 9, respectively.
** With 666 objects, 伐折羅-vajra-'s MEDIUM chart currently has the second highest number of objects in a MEDIUM chart, behind [[Rebellio]]'s 689.
** With 999 objects, 伐折羅-vajra-'s HARD chart currently has the fourth highest number of objects in a HARD chart, behind Rebellio's, [[onslaught]]'s, and [[V2|V₂]]'s 1073, 1014, and 1000, respectively.
* 伐折羅-vajra- is a song part of the [[POLICY BREAK]] event. For more information on the dates it could be unlocked in the SOUND VOLTEX series, please see the event page.
** From September 12th, 2019 in [[AC SDVX VW|SOUND VOLTEX VIVID WAVE]] and from October 2nd, 2019 in [[CS SDVX III|SOUND VOLTEX III GRAVITY WARS コナステ]], it can be purchased with PCB instead.
* After being removed from the initial release of REFLEC BEAT 悠久のリフレシア, 伐折羅-vajra- was revived on February 2nd, 2017.
* 伐折羅-vajra- is available in SOUND VOLTEX III GRAVITY WARS コナステ's INFINITE course and [[CS SDVX EG|EXCEED GEAR コナステ]] from November 6th, 2019, by purchasing '''Konasute SOUND VOLTEX Music Pack vol.5''' (コナステ版 SOUND VOLTEX 楽曲パック vol.5).
* 伐折羅-vajra- is one of the ''North America Area'' songs of beatmania IIDX 28 BISTROVER's ''Meshimase! BISTROVER'' (召しませ！BISTROVER) unlocking system. Its charts could be unlocked from May 10th, 2021.
** From February 14th, 2022, its charts could be purchased in [[AC CastHour|beatmania IIDX 29 CastHour]] with [[AC CastHour/Archive Links|Archive Links]] (アーカイブリンク).
** As of [[AC RESIDENT|beatmania IIDX 30 RESIDENT]], it is available by default.
* 伐折羅-vajra- is available in DanceDanceRevolution GRAND PRIX's GRAND PRIX mode from April 24th, 2023, by purchasing '''SPECIAL music pack feat.REFLEC BEAT vol.2''' (スペシャル楽曲パック feat.REFLEC BEAT vol.2).
** Its CHALLENGE charts become available by purchasing both this and '''SPECIAL music pack feat.REFLEC BEAT vol.2''' (スペシャル楽曲パック feat.REFLEC BEAT vol.1).
** By purchasing both packs with an active subscription, 伐折羅-vajra- and its CHALLENGE charts can be played in DanceDanceRevolution A3.
** From April 30th, 2024 in DanceDanceRevolution A3, it is available by default for all players.
* In DanceDanceRevolution A3 and GRAND PRIX, 伐折羅-vajra-'s BPM is listed as 87-173.
* 伐折羅-vajra- appears as selectable background music in ''CHASE CHASE JOKERS'' (チェイスチェイスジョーカーズ).
* 伐折羅-vajra- was added to [[CS ULTIMATE MOBILE|beatmania IIDX ULTIMATE MOBILE]] on March 20th, 2025.

