== Song Connections / Remixes ==
* 50th Memorial Songs -The BEMANI History- is a remixed medley of songs from the [[beatmania Information|beatmania]], [[beatmania IIDX Information|beatmania IIDX]], [[DanceDanceRevolution Information|DanceDanceRevolution]], [[GITADORA Information|DrumMania, GuitarFreaks]], and [[pop'n music Information|pop'n music]] BEMANI series.
** The songs, in order of appearance: [[e-motion ~ROMANTIC STYLE~|e-motion ～ROMANTIC STYLE～]] ([[AC bm CORE REMIX|beatmania CORE REMIX]]), [[Camomile bathroom|カモミール・バスルーム]] ([[AC pnm 7|pop'n music 7]]), [[Tangerine Stream]] ([[AC 3rd style|beatmania IIDX 3rd style]]) and [[Homesick Pt.2&3]] ([[AC pnm 5|pop'n music 5]]), [[PARANOiA]] and [[TRIP MACHINE]] ([[AC DDR 1st|DanceDanceRevolution]]), [[IMPLANTATION]] ([[AC DM2|drummania 2ndMIX]]), [[Daikenkai|大見解]] ([[AC pnm 6|pop'n music 6]]), [[One More Lovely]] ([[AC 10th style|beatmania IIDX 10th style]]), [[murmur twins]] ([[AC 8th style|beatmania IIDX 8th style]]), [[The Least 100sec]] ([[AC GF5DM4|GUITARFREAKS 5thMIX & drummania 4thMIX]]), [[I REALLY WANT TO HURT YOU]] ([[AC pnm|pop'n music]]), [[ABSOLUTE]] ([[AC 4th style|beatmania IIDX 4th style]]), [[Cutie pie]] ([[AC GF|GUITARFREAKS]]), and [[e-motion]] ([[AC bm 1st|beatmania]]).
** Part of the melody before PARANOiA is taken from the KONAMI title screen jingle heard in Japanese region console games released from 1995 to 1998, which was later arranged as [[MAKE A JAM!]] and [[mosaic]].
** The "Get on the dance floor" sample was used in the title BGM of [[AC DDR 2nd|DanceDanceRevolution 2ndMIX]], as well as the title BGMs used in earlier beatmania IIDX games, from [[AC 1st style|beatmania IIDX]] to [[AC 4th style|beatmania IIDX 4th style]].

== Trivia ==
{{Gallery}}
* 50th Memorial Songs -The BEMANI History- is the fourth song of the ''KONAMI 50th Anniversary Memorial Songs'' event. It was added to all participating BEMANI arcade games as a default song on April 25th, 2019, except for the following series:
** In GITADORA, it is one of the unlocks of GITADORA EXCHAIN's ''Memorial campaign'' (メモリアルキャンペーン) event. It could be unlocked from April 25th to May 22nd, 2019.
*** From December 28th, 2020, it could be unlocked from [[AC GD NEX+AGE|GITADORA NEX+AGE]] to [[AC GD HIGH-VOLTAGE|HIGH-VOLTAGE]] by clearing it in [[DX Challenge|Deluxe Mode]].
*** As of [[AC GD FUZZ-UP|GITADORA FUZZ-UP]], it is available by default.
** In jubeat, it is one of the unlocks of jubeat festo's ''E-emo STORE''. It could be purchased from April 25th to May 22nd, 2019 with 200 E-emo.
*** It could be purchased again with 100 T-emo from November 5th to December 2nd, 2019, and from May 7th to July 6th, 2020.
*** From [[AC jb Ave.|jubeat Ave.]] onwards, it is available by default with an [[e-amusement]] pass.
** In pop'n music peace, it is one of the unlocks of the ''pop'n time trip'' (ポップンタイムトリップ) event. It could be unlocked from April 25th, 2019 to February 19th, 2020 by filling out the second KONAMI 50th stamp card.
*** As of September 30th, 2020, it is available by default.
** In ノスタルジア Op.2, it is part of the ''Anniversary island'' (アニバーサリーアイランド) event. It can be unlocked by collecting 222 stamps.
*** In [[AC NST Op.3|ノスタルジア Op.3]], it can be unlocked from June 11th, 2020 from the [[AC NST Op.3/Old Hidden Songs|ノスタルジアFORTE&Op.2 イベント]] section at the Episode selection screen.
* In pop'n music, if the player chooses Mimi [pe-1P] as their character and plays 50th Memorial Songs -The BEMANI History-, the rival character will be Nyami [pe-1P] instead of her.
** Instead of displaying its character's portrait, 50th Memorial Songs -The BEMANI History- displays its jacket on the song selection screen.
* 50th Memorial Songs -The BEMANI History- marks Yuya Yokoyama's first appearance in the DanceDanceRevolution and SOUND VOLTEX series.
* Prior to [[AC DDR WORLD|DanceDanceRevolution WORLD]], 50th Memorial Songs -The BEMANI History-'s music video eliminates any on-screen dancers.
* 50th Memorial Songs -The BEMANI History- does not appear in the European release of DanceDanceRevolution A.
* The SOUND VOLTEX effector credits for 50th Memorial Songs -The BEMANI History- reference the [[Wikipedia:Konami Code|KONAMI code]].
* In SOUND VOLTEX III GRAVITY WARS コナステ, 50th Memorial Songs -The BEMANI History-'s VIVID chart appears instead as a GRAVITY chart. It was later changed back to VIVID in [[CS SDVX EG|SOUND VOLTEX EXCEED GEAR コナステ]]
* 50th Memorial Songs -The BEMANI History-'s jacket artist is uncredited in the SOUND VOLTEX series.
* In REFLEC BEAT, the PARANOiA and TRIP MACHINE part of 50th Memorial Songs -The BEMANI History- scrolls at half speed.
* 50th Memorial Songs -The BEMANI History- is available in [[CS GD Konasute|コナステ GITADORA]] by purchasing '''Konasute GITADORA Tokubetsu kikaku SELECTION PACK vol.2''' (コナステ GITADORA 特別企画セレクションパック vol.2).
* 50th Memorial Songs -The BEMANI History- is available in [[CS DDR GRAND PRIX|DanceDanceRevolution GRAND PRIX]]'s GRAND PRIX mode from August 7th, 2024, by purchasing '''GRAND PRIX music pack vol.30''' (グランプリ楽曲パック vol.30).
* 50th Memorial Songs -The BEMANI History- is available in [[CS pnm Lively|pop'n music Lively]] by purchasing '''pop'n music Lively Selection Music Pack vol.4''' (pop'n music Lively セレクション 楽曲パック vol.4).
* 50th Memorial Songs -The BEMANI History- received a BEGINNER chart in [[AC Pinky Crush|beatmania IIDX 32 Pinky Crush]].
** This chart was added to [[CS INFINITAS 2020|beatmania IIDX INFINITAS (2020)]] on December 18th, 2024.
* The banner for 50th Memorial Songs -The BEMANI History- in the pop'n music series misspelled the title as '''50th 50th Memorial Songs -The BEMANI History-'''. This was fixed in [[AC pnm High Cheers!!|pop'n music High☆Cheers!!]] on March 31st, 2026.

