== Song Connections / Remixes ==
* The original full version of Firestorm appears on Lilium Records' [[Blaze Bullet]] free album.
* An updated, long version of Firestorm, titled ''Firestorm 2K16'', appears on ETIA.'s fourth album, [[IKAROS]].
* Firestorm shares the background voice samples with [[ULTRA HAPPY MEGAMIX]].
* Firestorm was performed live as part of the ''AUTOMATION PARADISE ～[[Yasutomo Hirama|MAD CHILD]] SPECIAL MIX～'' medley at [[KONAMI Arcade Championship|The 8th KONAMI Arcade Championship]].

== Trivia ==
* Firestorm is a song part of ''The First VOLTEX Character Theme Song Contest'' (第一回ボルテキャラテーマ曲コンテスト). It was added to SOUND VOLTEX III GRAVITY WARS on September 17th, 2015.
* Firestorm's character is [[Nishinippori-san]].
** [[Sakurako Sobani]], [[Mitsuruko-chan]], [[Kureha]], and [[TSUBAKI & KUROMIMIPANDA|TSUBAKI]] appear in Firestorm's ADVANCED and EXHAUST jackets.
* Firestorm uses the series' fire background. Nishinippori, Firestorm's character, appears halfway into the song.
* Firestorm's EXHAUST chart can be purchased in SOUND VOLTEX III GRAVITY WARS after clearing [[Shanghai Wu Long|Shanghai Wu Long ～上海舞龍～]]'s EXHAUST chart with an A rank or above.
** Firestorm's ADVANCED chart can be purchased after simply clearing Shanghai Wu Long ～上海舞龍～'s ADVANCED chart.
** Since [[AC SDVX IV|SOUND VOLTEX IV HEAVENLY HAVEN]], its EXHAUST chart can also be purchased after playing Shanghai Wu Long ～上海舞龍～'s EXHAUST chart ten times, while its ADVANCED chart is available by default.
* Firestorm is one of the songs in Part 38 of [[FLOOR INFECTION]]. During its periods of availability, it could be unlocked in the DanceDanceRevolution series by playing 5 rounds of the corresponding SOUND VOLTEX series game to raise the ''infection level'' to Level 2 MAX. For more information on the dates it could be unlocked, please see the event page.
** Firestorm being crossed over marks ETIA.'s first appearance in the DanceDanceRevolution series.
** From [[AC DDR A3|DanceDanceRevolution A3]] onwards, it is available by default.
* Firestorm's EXHAUST jacket is used as its jacket in the DanceDanceRevolution series.
* Firestorm received CHALLENGE charts as part of [[AC DDR A20 PLUS|DanceDanceRevolution A20 PLUS]]' ''DDR CHALLENGE Carnival PLUS'' event. They could be unlocked from August 3rd to December 8th, 2020 after obtaining 16 stamps.
** From DanceDanceRevolution A3 onwards, they are available by default.
* Firestorm's Single CHALLENGE chart currently has the third highest number of Shock Arrows on Single Play, with 122 Shock Arrows, behind the Single CHALLENGE charts of [[Battle Against a True Hero / Honmono no hero to no tatakai|Battle Against a True Hero]] and [[Touch My Body]], with 147 and 140 Shock Arrows, respectively.

