== Trivia ==
{{Gallery}}
* Fly far bounce was added to DanceDanceRevolution A, MÚSECA 1+1/2, pop'n music うさぎと猫と少年の夢, and SOUND VOLTEX IV HEAVENLY HAVEN on March 15th, 2017, as part of the ''NOSTALGIA launch memorial song crossover campaign'' (ノスタルジア稼働記念 楽曲交換キャンペーン).
** It marks the first time ''any'' of these series receive a ノスタルジア crossover.
** In pop'n music, instead of displaying its character's portrait, Fly far bounce displays its jacket on the song selection screen.
* Despite displaying its BPM as a constant 163 BPM in pre-[[AC DDR WORLD|DanceDanceRevolution WORLD]] installments, as well as in [[CS DDR GRAND PRIX|DanceDanceRevolution GRAND PRIX]], Fly far bounce in the DanceDanceRevolution series has a slowdown at the very end of the song, much like in the other BEMANI games.
* In the DanceDanceRevolution series, while playing Fly far bounce, the crowd does not cheer. The announcer still talks, though.
* Fly far bounce ranked #1 in the BEMANI Fan Site CHECK!SONGS Monthly Ranking list for March 2017.
* Fly far bounce was added to GITADORA Tri-Boost Re:EVOLVE on March 15th, 2017, as part of the ''NOSTALGIA launch memorial song crossover campaign'' (ノスタルジア稼働記念 楽曲交換キャンペーン).
** It marks the first time the GuitarFreaks & DrumMania series receive a ノスタルジア crossover.
* In jubeat plus, Fly far bounce's EXTREME chart was slightly modified on August 15th, 2017.
* Fly far bounce is one of the unlocks of jubeat clan's ''import SHOP Tic-Tac'' SHOP. It could be unlocked from October 26th to November 15th, 2017. It can be purchased with 7 よいRED and 7 よいPLUM MIYAGEs.
** It could be purchased again from January 18th to February 7th, 2018, and from August 16th to September 2nd, 2018.
** In [[AC jb festo|jubeat festo]], it can be purchased at the ''emo MART''.
** From [[AC jb Ave.|jubeat Ave.]] onwards, it is available by default with an [[e-amusement]] pass.
* Fly far bounce received a Real chart in [[AC NST Op.2|ノスタルジア Op.2]].
* Fly far bounce was added to [[CS SDVX III|SOUND VOLTEX III GRAVITY WARS コナステ]]'s REGULAR course on August 1st, 2019.
* At the end of Fly far bounce in earlier versions of the SOUND VOLTEX series, the chain counter would glitch and not count the LONG notes properly. This bug was fixed in [[AC SDVX EG|SOUND VOLTEX EXCEED GEAR]].
** This might have been caused by the quick BPM changes, as the chain count of LONG notes relies on the song's BPM.
** When the BPM is shown as 162, 161, and 160, the actual BPM rapidly decrease in decimals every one-sixteenth of a measure.
* Fly far bounce's [[CS jb 2021|jubeat (2021)]] ratings were adjusted to its jubeat festo ratings on March 7th, 2022.
* Fly far bounce is available in [[CS GD Konasute|コナステ GITADORA]] by purchasing '''Konasute GITADORA HISTORY PACK vol.3''' (コナステ GITADORA HISTORYパック vol.3).
* Fly far bounce is available in DanceDanceRevolution GRAND PRIX's GRAND PRIX mode from February 20th, 2023, by purchasing '''GRAND PRIX music pack vol.15''' (グランプリ楽曲パック vol.15).
* Fly far bounce is available in [[CS SDVX EG|SOUND VOLTEX EXCEED GEAR コナステ]] from December 9th, 2023, by purchasing '''Konasute SOUND VOLTEX Music Pack vol.21''' (コナステ版 SOUND VOLTEX 楽曲パック vol.21).

