== Trivia ==
{{Gallery}}
* Chinese Snowy Dance is GuitarFreaksXG2 & DrumManiaXG2's and GuitarFreaks V8 & DrumMania V8's ENCORE STAGE at Extra Level 1. 
** As of Extra Level 2 (April 15th, 2011), it has moved down to EXTRA STAGE.
* Chinese Snowy Dance was performed at ''THE GITADO LIVE 2011'' concert, held in Tokyo and Osaka in 2011.
* According to Mutsuhiko Izumi, he would like to make a vocal version of Chinese Snowy Dance.
* Chinese Snowy Dance is the second FINAL STAGE song of REFLEC BEAT colette -Winter-.
** From [[AC RB groovin'!!|REFLEC BEAT groovin'!!]] to [[AC RB VOLZZA 2|REFLEC BEAT VOLZZA 2]], it was playable by default.
* Chinese Snowy Dance was added to DanceDanceRevolution (2013) on August 26th, 2013 as part of the [[jubeat-GITADORA-DDR no Triple Journey|jubeat・GITADORA・DDRのTriple Journey]] unlock event, which started on August 1st, 2013.
** To unlock Chinese Snowy Dance on DanceDanceRevolution, while on the total results screen, press in order Up, Up, Down, Down, Left, Right, Left, Right on the pad, and then press the Left, Right buttons of the machine itself.
*** This is a reference to the [[Wikipedia:Konami Code|KONAMI Code]] (↑↑↓↓←→←→B A START).
*** In the August 26th mail on the Triple Journey site, [[BABY-LON]] is seen flying through one of the stages in the video game ''GRADIUS'', where the KONAMI Code came from.
** From October 1st, 2013, it could be unlocked in DanceDanceRevolution (2013) and [[AC DDR 2014|DanceDanceRevolution (2014)]] by playing eleven rounds with an [[e-amusement|eAMUSEMENT]] PASS.
** From [[AC DDR A|DanceDanceRevolution A]] onwards, it is playable by default.
* After being removed from the initial release of [[AC RB Reflesia|REFLEC BEAT 悠久のリフレシア]], Chinese Snowy Dance was revived on May 16th, 2019.
