== Trivia ==
* GAIA is one of the [[Shiritsu BEMANI gakuen]] (私立BEMANI学園) songs. To unlock it, you must get 100% of Friendship on L.E.D. and Nekomata Master. After the event ended, it can be unlocked through different systems, depending on the BEMANI game:
** In [[AC SPADA|beatmania IIDX 21 SPADA]], it could be automatically unlocked after 3 play sessions until July 24th, 2014.
*** From July 24th, 2014 up until June 25th, 2015, it could be unlocked via the [[Hakken! Yomigaetta BEMANI iseki|発見！よみがえったBEMANI遺跡]] event in beatmania IIDX 21 SPADA and [[AC PENDUAL|beatmania IIDX 22 PENDUAL]].
*** Since July 1st, 2015 in beatmania IIDX 22 PENDUAL, it could be obtained by purchasing the ''BEMANI学園'' pack (which includes all 私立BEMANI学園 songs) for 7000 FRICO.
*** From [[AC copula|beatmania IIDX 23 copula]] onwards, it is available by default.
** In DanceDanceRevolution (2013) and [[AC DDR 2014|DanceDanceRevolution (2014)]], it could be automatically unlocked after 4 play sessions.
*** From [[AC DDR A|DanceDanceRevolution A]] onwards, it is available by default.
** In jubeat saucer, it could be unlocked via the ''bistro saucer'' unlocking system.
*** In [[AC jb saucer fulfill|jubeat saucer fulfill]], it could be unlocked as part of ''saucer macchiato'''s Side Menu from April 23rd, 2014.
*** In [[AC jb prop|jubeat prop]], it could be unlocked by playing it as a BONUS TUNE from May 28th, 2015.
*** As of [[AC jb Qubell|jubeat Qubell]], it is available by default by playing with an [[e-amusement]] pass.
** In pop'n music Sunny Park, it could be unlocked in the [[AC pnm Sunny Park/Waiwai pop'n doubutsuen|Waiwai pop'n doubutsuen]] (わいわいポップン動物園) unlocking event from December 19th, 2013.
*** In [[AC pnm Lapistoria|pop'n music ラピストリア]], it could be unlocked via Story Mode from July 9th, 2014.
*** In [[AC pnm eclale|pop'n music éclale]], it could be purchased from the Star Factory shop for 60 lumina.
*** As of [[AC pnm Usaneko|pop'n music うさぎと猫と少年の夢]], it is available by default.
** In [[AC RB colette All Seasons|REFLEC BEAT colette -All Seasons-]], it could be unlocked after a play session.
*** From [[AC RB groovin'!!|REFLEC BEAT groovin'!!]] to [[AC RB VOLZZA 2|VOLZZA 2]], it was unlocked by default.
* GAIA marks the first collaboration between Naoyuki Sato and Toshiyuki Kakuta in BEMANI.
** It also marks the first appearance of Naoyuki Sato's 猫叉Master+ alias in pop'n music.
* In DanceDanceRevolution, GAIA's EXPERT charts are the only charts rated Level 16 or higher with no jumps or Freeze Arrows in them.
* Gaia or Gaea (pronounced "gee-uh" or "gey-uh") is the Greek word for "earth". It also refers to the Greek goddess of the Earth, who was the mother of the Titans and cyclopes.
* Despite that MZD has a new design, none of the 私立BEMANI学園 songs have new comments on the pop'n music Sunny Park MUSIC&CHARACTERS page.
* In GAIA's jacket and in jukebeat, GAIA's artist is romanized as '''Nekomata L.E.D.Master+'''.
* GAIA was one of the qualifying round songs in the [[KONAMI Arcade Championship|KONAMI Arcade Championship 2013]] for DanceDanceRevolution (2013).
* After being removed from the initial release of [[AC RB Reflesia|REFLEC BEAT 悠久のリフレシア]], GAIA was revived on August 3rd, 2017.
** Its WHITE HARD chart could be unlocked through a quest in Reflesia Mode (リフレシアモード) from August 17th to 30th, 2017.
*** Since March 8th, 2018, it is available by default.
* GAIA could be unlocked in SOUND VOLTEX IV HEAVENLY HAVEN by collecting 20 stamps from October 4th to October 28th, 2018.
** In [[AC SDVX VW|SOUND VOLTEX VIVID WAVE]], it can be purchased with PCB from June 27th, 2019.
* GAIA is available in [[CS INFINITAS|beatmania IIDX INFINITAS]] by purchasing '''beatmania IIDX INFINITAS Music Pack vol.5''' (beatmania IIDX INFINITAS 楽曲パック vol.5).
* GAIA was added to [[CS SDVX III|SOUND VOLTEX III GRAVITY WARS コナステ]]'s REGULAR course on August 1st, 2019.
** It is also available in GRAVITY WARS コナステ's INFINITE course and [[CS SDVX EG|EXCEED GEAR コナステ]] from February 5th, 2020, by purchasing '''Konasute SOUND VOLTEX Music Pack vol.8''' (コナステ版 SOUND VOLTEX 楽曲パック vol.8).
* GAIA is available in [[CS NST Konasute|コナステ ノスタルジア]] by purchasing '''Konasute NOSTALGIA Music Pack vol.5 ～Shiritsu BEMANI gakuen～''' (コナステ ノスタルジア 楽曲パック vol.5 ～私立BEMANI学園～).
* GAIA is one of the unlocks of ノスタルジア Op.3's ''Toki wo meguru ongaku-sai Vol.III'' (時を巡る音楽祭　Vol.III) event, initially available for unlock from August 19th to October 21st, 2021 (originally until September 30th, 2021). For more information on the dates when the event was revived, please see [[AC NST Op.3#Toki wo meguru ongaku-sai|this page]].
** From October 10th, 2024, it is permanently available for unlock.
* GAIA received a Real chart in ノスタルジア Op.3 on August 19th, 2021.
* GAIA is available in [[CS DDR GRAND PRIX|DanceDanceRevolution GRAND PRIX]]'s GRAND PRIX mode from March 1st, 2022, by purchasing '''GRAND PRIX music pack vol.3''' (グランプリ楽曲パック vol.3).
* GAIA's [[CS jb 2021|jubeat (2021)]] ratings were adjusted to its jubeat festo ratings on March 7th, 2022.
* GAIA is available in [[CS pnm Lively|pop'n music Lively]] by purchasing '''pop'n music Lively Music Pack vol.14''' (pop'n music Lively 楽曲パック vol.14).
* GAIA is one of the unlocks of ポラリスコード's ''Hakkutsu! Caravan universe'' (発掘！キャラバンユニバース) event, through the ''BEMANI gakuen -shotoubu- location'' (BEMANI学園-初等部-ロケ) route. It can be unlocked from March 27th, 2025.
* GAIA's INFLUENCE chart was re-rated in ポラリスコード on March 23rd, 2026.

