== Trivia ==
* STULTI is one of the [[Shiritsu BEMANI gakuen]] (私立BEMANI学園) songs. To unlock it, obtain 100% of Friendship on MAX MAXIMIZER and DJ TOTTO. After the event ended, it can be unlocked through different systems, depending on the BEMANI game:
** In [[AC SPADA|beatmania IIDX 21 SPADA]], it could be automatically unlocked after 6 play sessions until July 24th, 2014.
*** From July 24th, 2014 up until June 25th, 2015, it could be unlocked via the [[Hakken! Yomigaetta BEMANI iseki|発見！よみがえったBEMANI遺跡]] event in beatmania IIDX 21 SPADA and [[AC PENDUAL|beatmania IIDX 22 PENDUAL]].
*** Since July 1st, 2015 in beatmania IIDX 22 PENDUAL, it could be obtained by purchasing the ''BEMANI学園'' pack (which includes all 私立BEMANI学園 songs) for 7000 FRICO.
*** From [[AC copula|beatmania IIDX 23 copula]] onwards, it is available by default.
** In DanceDanceRevolution (2013) and [[AC DDR 2014|DanceDanceRevolution (2014)]], it could be automatically unlocked after 5 play sessions.
*** From [[AC DDR A|DanceDanceRevolution A]] onwards, it is available by default.
** In GITADORA, it could be unlocked for 5000 Live Pts. from December 19th, 2013.
*** In [[AC GD OverDrive|GITADORA OverDrive]], it is available by default for new players with an [[e-amusement|eAMUSEMENT]] PASS.
*** As of the end of March 2014 in GITADORA OverDrive, it is available by default for all players.
** In jubeat saucer, it could be unlocked via the ''bistro saucer'' unlocking system.
*** In [[AC jb saucer fulfill|jubeat saucer fulfill]], it could be unlocked as part of ''saucer macchiato'''s Side Menu from April 23rd, 2014.
*** In [[AC jb prop|jubeat prop]], it could be unlocked by playing it as a BONUS TUNE from May 28th, 2015.
*** As of [[AC jb Qubell|jubeat Qubell]], it is available by default by playing with an [[e-amusement]] pass.
** In pop'n music Sunny Park, it could be unlocked in the [[AC pnm Sunny Park/Waiwai pop'n doubutsuen|Waiwai pop'n doubutsuen]] (わいわいポップン動物園) unlocking event from December 19th, 2013.
*** In [[AC pnm Lapistoria|pop'n music ラピストリア]], it could be unlocked via Story Mode from July 9th, 2014.
*** In [[AC pnm eclale|pop'n music éclale]], it could be purchased from the Star Factory shop for 60 lumina.
*** As of [[AC pnm Usaneko|pop'n music うさぎと猫と少年の夢]], it is available by default.
** In [[AC RB colette All Seasons|REFLEC BEAT colette -All Seasons-]], it could be unlocked after a play session.
*** From [[AC RB groovin'!!|REFLEC BEAT groovin'!!]] to [[AC RB VOLZZA 2|VOLZZA 2]], it was unlocked by default.
* STULTI marks the first collaboration between Tatsuya Iyama and Yoshihiro Tagawa in BEMANI.
** It also marks Tatsuya Iyama's first use of his MAX MAXIMIZER alias outside the beatmania IIDX or REFLEC BEAT series.
** It also marks Yoshihiro Tagawa's debut on the beatmania IIDX, DanceDanceRevolution, GuitarFreaks & DrumMania, jubeat, and pop'n music series.
* "Stulti" is Latin for "fool".
* STULTI's genre, GRAVIOL, is a corruption of the Latin word "gravior", which means "heavy".
* Despite that MZD has a new design, none of the 私立BEMANI学園 songs have new comments on the pop'n music Sunny Park MUSIC&CHARACTERS page.
* STULTI's BPM was displayed as just 182 in REFLEC BEAT colette -Spring-. This was corrected to 90-182 in [[AC RB colette Summer|REFLEC BEAT colette -Summer-]].
** It is displayed as 90-192 in REFLEC BEAT plus.
* Due to the ''私立BEMANI学園 ORIGINAL SOUNDTRACK'' being released before the ''REFLEC BEAT colette ORIGINAL SOUNDTRACK vol.2'' (which included Yoshihiro Tagawa's first BEMANI song, [[Valanga]]), STULTI is the first song of his to appear on a BEMANI original soundtrack.
* STULTI was one of the qualifying round songs in the [[KONAMI Arcade Championship|KONAMI Arcade Championship 2013]] for DanceDanceRevolution (2013).
* STULTI was automatically added to [[CS GD|GITADORA (Mobile)]]'s Collection Mode for every player on September 28th, 2013 (you still need to buy it, though.)
* STULTI's EASY chart was re-rated in pop'n music éclale on March 22nd, 2016.
* STULTI's timing was slightly fixed on the October 4th, 2016 update of [[AC DDR A|DanceDanceRevolution A]].
* After being removed from the initial release of [[AC RB Reflesia|REFLEC BEAT 悠久のリフレシア]], STULTI was revived on February 2nd, 2017.
* STULTI could be unlocked in SOUND VOLTEX IV HEAVENLY HAVEN by collecting 25 stamps from October 4th to October 28th, 2018.
** In [[AC SDVX VW|SOUND VOLTEX VIVID WAVE]], it can be purchased with PCB from June 27th, 2019.
* STULTI is available in [[CS INFINITAS|beatmania IIDX INFINITAS]] by purchasing '''beatmania IIDX INFINITAS Music Pack vol.5''' (beatmania IIDX INFINITAS 楽曲パック vol.5).
* STULTI's difficulty level change from [[AC DDR A20|DanceDanceRevolution A20]] was applied to DanceDanceRevolution A on March 27th, 2019.
* STULTI was added to [[CS SDVX III|SOUND VOLTEX III GRAVITY WARS コナステ]]'s REGULAR course on August 1st, 2019.
** It is also available in GRAVITY WARS コナステ's INFINITE course and [[CS SDVX EG|EXCEED GEAR コナステ]] from January 8th, 2020, by purchasing '''Konasute SOUND VOLTEX Music Pack vol.7''' (コナステ版 SOUND VOLTEX 楽曲パック vol.7).
* STULTI is available in [[CS NST Konasute|コナステ ノスタルジア]] by purchasing '''Konasute NOSTALGIA Music Pack vol.5 ～Shiritsu BEMANI gakuen～''' (コナステ ノスタルジア 楽曲パック vol.5 ～私立BEMANI学園～).
* STULTI is one of the unlocks of ノスタルジア Op.3's ''Toki wo meguru ongaku-sai Vol.III'' (時を巡る音楽祭　Vol.III) event, initially available for unlock from September 2nd to October 21st, 2021 (originally until September 30th, 2021). For more information on the dates when the event was revived, please see [[AC NST Op.3#Toki wo meguru ongaku-sai|this page]].
** From October 10th, 2024, it is permanently available for unlock.
* STULTI is available in [[CS DDR GRAND PRIX|DanceDanceRevolution GRAND PRIX]]'s GRAND PRIX mode from March 1st, 2022, by purchasing '''GRAND PRIX music pack vol.3''' (グランプリ楽曲パック vol.3).
* STULTI's [[CS jb 2021|jubeat (2021)]] ratings were adjusted to its jubeat festo ratings on March 7th, 2022.
* STULTI is available in [[CS GD Konasute|コナステ GITADORA]] by purchasing '''Konasute GITADORA HISTORY PACK vol.18''' (コナステ GITADORA HISTORYパック vol.18).
* STULTI is available in [[CS pnm Lively|pop'n music Lively]] by purchasing '''pop'n music Lively Music Pack vol.14''' (pop'n music Lively 楽曲パック vol.14).
* STULTI is one of the unlocks of ポラリスコード's ''Hakkutsu! Caravan universe'' (発掘！キャラバンユニバース) event, through the ''BEMANI gakuen -chuutoubu- location'' (BEMANI学園-中等部-ロケ) route. It can be unlocked from March 27th, 2025.
* STULTI's INFLUENCE chart was re-rated in ポラリスコード on March 23rd, 2026.

