== Song Connections / Remixes ==
* デッドボヲルdeホームラン is slightly remixed in GITADORA, with more emphasis on guitars.
* デッドボヲルdeホームラン shares similarities with [[Funny shuffle]], from beatmania IIDX 21 SPADA.
* The string sound from the very end of [[CALL]] can be heard at the end of デッドボヲルdeホームラン.
* The ノスタルジア series uses a slightly rearranged version of デッドボヲルdeホームラン, featuring additional piano arrangement by [[Akhuta]].

== Trivia ==
* デッドボヲルdeホームラン is one of the songs part of the Second Half of the [[Nettou! BEMANI Stadium]] (熱闘！BEMANIスタジアム) event.
** In [[AC DDR A|DanceDanceRevolution A]], it can be unlocked through ''EXTRA SAVIOR''.
*** As of [[AC DDR A20|DanceDanceRevolution A20]], it is available by default.
** In [[AC jb saucer fulfill|jubeat saucer fulfill]], it can be unlocked as part of ''saucer macchiato'''s Side Menu from August 26th, 2014.
*** In [[AC jb prop|jubeat prop]], it can be unlocked by playing it as a BONUS TUNE from May 28th, 2015.
*** In [[AC jb Qubell|jubeat Qubell]], it is one of the Garnet unlocks of the ''dig dig Qubell'' unlocking system.
*** In [[AC jb clan|jubeat clan]], it can be unlocked in the ''jubeat SHOP''.
*** In [[AC jb festo|jubeat festo]], it can be purchased at the ''emo MART''.
*** From [[AC jb Ave.|jubeat Ave.]] onwards, it is available by default with an [[e-amusement]] pass.
** From March 16th, 2015, it could be unlocked in [[AC pnm Lapistoria|pop'n music ラピストリア]] via Story Mode.
*** In [[AC pnm eclale|pop'n music éclale]], it could be purchased from the Star Factory shop for 60 lumina.
*** As of [[AC pnm Usaneko|pop'n music うさぎと猫と少年の夢]], it is available by default.
** In [[AC RB groovin'!!|REFLEC BEAT groovin'!!]] and [[AC RB groovin'!! Upper|REFLEC BEAT groovin'!! Upper]], デッドボヲルdeホームラン can be purchased from the REFLEC Shop after clearing it in the BEMANI Stadium Test (BEMANIスタジアム検定) added on July 24th, 2014.
*** In [[AC RB VOLZZA|REFLEC BEAT VOLZZA]] and [[AC RB VOLZZA 2|REFLEC BEAT VOLZZA 2]], デッドボヲルdeホームラン is playable by default.
* デッドボヲルdeホームラン marks the first usage of Naoyuki Sato's 猫叉Masterβ2 alias outside of pop'n music.
** It also marks Naoyuki Sato's first original song in the SOUND VOLTEX and ミライダガッキ FutureTomTom series.
*** It also marks his debut in the SOUND VOLTEX series.
* In pop'n music, instead of displaying its character's portrait, デッドボヲルdeホームラン displays its jacket (with the 熱闘！BEMANIスタジアム logo) when selected.
* When デッドボヲルdeホームラン is played on beatmania IIDX, the arcade LED ticker displays "I LIKE DEADBALL".
** In jukebeat, デッドボヲルdeホームラン's title and artist were changed to '''I like deadball.''' and '''Nekomata_masterβ2''', respectively..
* デッドボヲルdeホームラン's jubeat charts were created by RAG [https://p.eagate.573.jp/game/bemani/fansite/p/report/2014w/report12.html?page=8].
* From [[AC DDR 2014|DanceDanceRevolution (2014)]] onwards, デッドボヲルdeホームラン appears in the DanceDanceRevolution (2014) folder instead of the (2013) folder.
* デッドボヲルdeホームラン received a SPECIAL chart in REFLEC BEAT groovin'!! on July 24th. 2014. It could be purchased from the REFLEC Shop for 1500 Refle, after clearing the chart in the FINAL ROUND of the BEMANI Stadium Test (BEMANIスタジアム検定) added on the same day.
** In REFLEC BEAT VOLZZA, it could be purchased from the Garage for 8 VOLZZA KEYs.
** In REFLEC BEAT VOLZZA 2, it could be unlocked by clearing its HARD chart a specific number of times, depending on the grade obtained on it (AAA+: 1 time, AAA: 2 times, AA: 3 times, A or lower: 5 times).
* デッドボヲルdeホームラン was shown to be revived in [[AC RB Reflesia|REFLEC BEAT 悠久のリフレシア]] on an in-game announcement on March 13th, 2019, despite the song not appearing in the game itself. The announcement was later removed.
** It was finally revived on June 20th, 2019.
* デッドボヲルdeホームラン was added to [[CS INFINITAS|beatmania IIDX INFINITAS]] on March 4th, 2020 as part of the March 2020 Basic Subscription Monthly Songs.
** From October 6th, 2021 in [[CS INFINITAS 2020|beatmania IIDX INFINITAS (2020)]], it can be purchased with [[CS INFINITAS/BIT unlocks|BITs]].
* デッドボヲルdeホームラン is one of the unlocks of ノスタルジア Op.3's ''Nettou! BEMANI Stadium'' (熱闘！BEMANIスタジアム) event, initially available for unlock from August 6th to 18th, 2020. For more information on the dates when the event was revived, please see [[AC NST Op.3#Nettou! BEMANI Stadium|this page]].
** From August 8th, 2024, it is permanently available for unlock.
* デッドボヲルdeホームラン received a Real chart in ノスタルジア Op.3 on September 23rd, 2020.
* デッドボヲルdeホームラン's [[CS jb 2021|jubeat (2021)]] ratings were adjusted to its jubeat festo ratings on March 7th, 2022.
* デッドボヲルdeホームラン is available in [[CS GD Konasute|コナステ GITADORA]] by purchasing '''Konasute GITADORA HISTORY PACK vol.18''' (コナステ GITADORA HISTORYパック vol.18).
* デッドボヲルdeホームラン is available in [[CS DDR GRAND PRIX|DanceDanceRevolution GRAND PRIX]]'s GRAND PRIX mode from August 22nd, 2022, by purchasing '''GRAND PRIX music pack vol.9''' (グランプリ楽曲パック vol.9).
* デッドボヲルdeホームラン received an EXCEED chart in [[AC SDVX EG|SOUND VOLTEX EXCEED GEAR]]'s [[AC SDVX EG/ARENA STATION|ARENA STATION]], available since May 2nd, 2024. For more information on the dates it can be unlocked, please see the event page.
** This chart is available in [[CS SDVX EG|SOUND VOLTEX EXCEED GEAR コナステ]] from March 26th, 2025, by purchasing '''Konasute SOUND VOLTEX EXCEED EFFECT Pack''' (コナステ版 SOUND VOLTEX EXCEED譜面パック).
* デッドボヲルdeホームラン is available in [[CS pnm Lively|pop'n music Lively]] by purchasing '''pop'n music Lively Selection Music Pack vol.4''' (pop'n music Lively セレクション 楽曲パック vol.4).
* デッドボヲルdeホームラン is one of the unlocks of ポラリスコード's ''Hakkutsu! Caravan universe'' (発掘！キャラバンユニバース) event, through the ''Nettou! BEMANI Stadium location ②'' (熱闘！BEMANIスタジアムロケ②) route. It can be unlocked from October 23rd, 2025.
* デッドボヲルdeホームラン's INFLUENCE chart was re-rated in ポラリスコード on March 23rd, 2026.

