== Song Connections / Remixes ==
* London EVOLVED is part of the "EVOLVED" song series.
* London EVOLVED has three different versions (London EVOLVED ver.A, ver.B, and ver.C), which share the same intro part.
** The REFLEC BEAT series uses London EVOLVED ver.A; however, it uses the regular London EVOLVED jacket instead of the ver.A variant.
** The ミライダガッキ FutureTomTom series uses London EVOLVED ver.C; however, it uses the regular London EVOLVED jacket instead of the ver.C variant.
* London EVOLVED is based on the background music for DanceDanceRevolution X2's PiX minigame.
* A remix of London EVOLVED by [[Yuichi Asami|2.1MB underground]], titled [[Tohoku EVOLVED]], appears in DanceDanceRevolution X3 VS 2ndMIX.
* London EVOLVED ver.C is one of the songs sampled in [[DDR TAGMIX -LAST DanceR-]], from [[AC DDR A20 PLUS|DanceDanceRevolution A20 PLUS]].
* London EVOLVED was performed live as part of the ''DanceDanceRevolution 20th Anniversary NONSTOP MEGAMIX'' medley at [[KONAMI Arcade Championship|The 7th KONAMI Arcade Championship]].

== Trivia ==
* London EVOLVED is one of the ''Replicant D-action'' hidden songs in DanceDanceRevolution II.
* In the DanceDanceRevolution master song list, London EVOLVED, under the title of '''Hi-End''', is listed between the songs from [[CS DDR HOTTEST PARTY3|DanceDanceRevolution HOTTEST PARTY3]] / [[CS DDR X2|DanceDanceRevolution X2 CS]], suggesting it was meant to appear in those games first.
** This association is confirmed by London EVOLVED's IDs, which are "hien1", "hien2" and "hien3".
* London EVOLVED was the fourth ''EXTRA TOUR'' song in DanceDanceRevolution X3 VS 2ndMIX. It could be played as an EXTRA STAGE since May 30th, 2012.
** In the arcade DanceDanceRevolution series, London EVOLVED's Ver.A, Ver.B, and Ver.C are capitalized as '''London EVOLVED ver.A''', '''ver.B''', and '''ver.C''', respectively.
** As of September 26th, 2012, London EVOLVED has been unlocked for normal play.
* London EVOLVED received new CHALLENGE charts in DanceDanceRevolution X3 VS 2ndMIX, replacing its old CHALLENGE charts from DanceDanceRevolution II.
* London EVOLVED is the 5th unlockable song of the ''Pastel Adventure'' colette Mountain 2 event of REFLEC BEAT colette -Winter-.
** From [[AC RB groovin'!!|REFLEC BEAT groovin'!!]] to [[AC RB VOLZZA 2|REFLEC BEAT VOLZZA 2]], London EVOLVED was playable by default.
* London EVOLVED is the first song of the EVOLVED series that has been crossed over into another BEMANI game.
* Prior to [[AC DDR WORLD|DanceDanceRevolution WORLD]], London EVOLVED's BPM was displayed as 170-340 for all of its versions. The actual BPM changes are as follows
** ver.A: 42.5-340 (170→340→170→340→stop→170→42.5→340→42.5)
** ver.B: 170-420 (170→340→170→340→stop→170→210→420→stop→420)
** ver.C: 170-340 (170→340→170→340→stop→340)
** In the REFLEC BEAT series, London EVOLVED's BPM was shown as 43-370. It has since been changed to 43-340 at an unknown date.
** London EVOLVED's BPM is also mistakenly displayed as 80-320 in DanceDanceRevolution II. No version runs at 80, 160 or 320 BPM.
* London EVOLVED ver.C was one of the qualifying round songs in the [[KONAMI Arcade Championship|KONAMI Arcade Championship 2013]] for [[AC DDR 2013|DanceDanceRevolution (2013)]].
* After being removed from the initial release of [[AC RB Reflesia|REFLEC BEAT 悠久のリフレシア]], London EVOLVED was revived on December 18th, 2019.
* London EVOLVED is available in [[CS DDR GRAND PRIX|DanceDanceRevolution GRAND PRIX]]'s GRAND PRIX mode from September 26th, 2024, by purchasing '''GRAND PRIX music pack vol.32''' (グランプリ楽曲パック vol.32).

