== Trivia ==
{{Gallery}}
* Sakura Sunrise is one of the ''Replicant D-action'' hidden songs in DanceDanceRevolution X2, representing the color green. To play Sakura Sunrise as a Replicant D-action song, you must clear at least 2 songs in each game folder (24 at least total).
** As of February 23rd, 2011, Sakura Sunrise has been unlocked for normal play.
* In pre-[[AC DDR WORLD|DanceDanceRevolution WORLD]] installments of the DanceDanceRevolution series, Sakura Sunrise's music video is shown in the background of a light blue-colored version of the REPLICANT background dance stage and is not full-screen.
** In [[CS DDR II|DanceDanceRevolution II / hottest party5]], Sakura Sunrise's video removes any on-screen dancers and is played in a tiny monitor on the opposite side of the player on Single and in the center on Double/Versus, due to Nintendo Wii memory limitations.
** This video reuses four DDRMAX-EXTREME background movies.
* Sakura Sunrise marks Ryutaro Nakahara's first original song for an arcade DanceDanceRevolution release.
** It also marks his first EXTRA STAGE song in DanceDanceRevolution.
* In the Japanese arcade version of DanceDanceRevolution X2, Sakura Sunrise had a slightly different jacket with a different font for "Ryu☆".
** This jacket is also used in the BeatStream and DANCE aROUND series.
* Sakura Sunrise appears as downloadable content for [[CS DDR S+|DanceDanceRevolution S+]], in the '''DDR X2 Special Pack'''.
* Sakura Sunrise is used as background music in a mission on the KONAMI arcade game ''ROAD FIGHTERS'' (ロードファイターズ).
* Sakura Sunrise is unlocked in REFLEC BEAT limelight by reaching the first part of Glass Stage 3-2.
** Sakura Sunrise is the first Replicant D-action song that has been crossed over to another BEMANI game.
** From [[AC RB colette|REFLEC BEAT colette]] to [[AC RB VOLZZA 2|REFLEC BEAT VOLZZA 2]], it was available by default.
* Sakura Sunrise is the final unlock of jubeat saucer's ''bistro saucer'' 6th Set. It could be unlocked from April 1st to 30th, 2013 after all other 6th Set songs are unlocked.
** It is the first bistro saucer final song in jubeat saucer that is a BEMANI crossover.
** It is also the only final song unlock from any bistro saucer set whose EXTREME chart is not rated Level 10.
