AFRONOVA:
= AFRONOVA =

== Song Information ==
[[Image:AFRONOVA.png|thumb|AFRONOVA's jacket.]]
Artist: RE-VENGE<br>
Composition/Arrangement: [[Naoki Maeda|NM SEQUENCE UNLIMITED]]<br>
BPM: 200<br>
Length: 1:29<br>
First Music Game Appearance: [[AC DDR 3rd|DanceDanceRevolution 3rdMIX]]<br>
Other Music Game Appearances: None.

== Lyrics ==
None.

== Song Connections / Remixes ==
* A portion of AFRONOVA is included in [[NONSTOP I]], from [[AC DDR Solo 2000|DanceDanceRevolution Solo 2000]].
* An 8-bit arrangement of AFRONOVA appears in [[CS DDR GB2|DanceDanceRevolution GB2]].
* A remix of AFRONOVA, titled [[AFRONOVA PRIMEVAL]], appears in [[AC DMX|Dance Maniax]].
* Another remix of AFRONOVA by B4 ZA BEAT, titled [[AFRONOVA(FROM NONSTOP MEGAMIX)]], appears in the [[DanceDanceRevolution 3rdMIX ORIGINAL SOUNDTRACK]] NONSTOP MEGAMIX. It was later included in [[AC DDRMAX2|DDRMAX2 -DanceDanceRevolution 7thMIX-]] as a CHALLENGE Mode-only playable edit of AFRONOVA.
* AFRONOVA shares tribal chanting samples with [[CRIES IN THE WILDERNESS]] and [[Debtty Daddy]].

== Trivia ==
{{Gallery}}
[[Image:Reese Witherspoon.jpg|thumb|100px|Reese Witherspoon's original photo.]]
* AFRONOVA marks Naoki Maeda's first use of his RE-VENGE (later RevenG) alias.
* AFRONOVA's EXPERT charts have a step pattern that was later known by the fans as "AFRONOVA walk", which is a long crossover section where the fourth note of the pattern starts another crossover, but is still an 8th note, instead of a 4th note.
** Despite that it became popular with AFRONOVA, [[SP-TRIP MACHINE~JUNGLE MIX~|SP-TRIP MACHINE～JUNGLE MIX～]]'s EXPERT charts used a shorter version of this pattern first.
* AFRONOVA's original background featured a modified photo of Reese Witherspoon. This background was changed in [[AC DDR 3rd PLUS|DanceDanceRevolution 3rdMIX PLUS]].
** AFRONOVA's jacket is based on the new background as well.
** In [[CS DDR Mini|DanceDanceRevolution Classic Mini]], AFRONOVA uses a placeholder background instead.
* AFRONOVA received a BEGINNER chart in [[AC DS EuroMIX|Dancing Stage EuroMIX]].
* AFRONOVA's EXPERT charts were slightly modified in [[AC DDR X|DanceDanceRevolution X]], fixing their quantization issues.
* '''AFRONOVA(X-Special)''' is one of the X-Special ENCORE EXTRA STAGEs in DanceDanceRevolution X, which could be played from May 7th, 2009 by obtaining at least a AA on [[PARANOiA Rebirth|PARANOiA Rebirth(X-Special)]] as the EXTRA STAGE.
** As of October 1st, 2009, AFRONOVA(X-Special) has been unlocked for normal play.
* From [[AC DDR X2|DanceDanceRevolution X2]] onwards, AFRONOVA(X-Special) appears in the DanceDanceRevolution X folder instead of the 3rdMIX folder.
* In DanceDanceRevolution GB2, AFRONOVA runs at 202 BPM.
* From June 1st, 2017 in [[AC DDR A|DanceDanceRevolution A]] to [[AC DDR A3|DanceDanceRevolution A3]], AFRONOVA(X-Special) does not appear in the song selection screen if the player does not use an [[e-amusement]] pass.
** From [[AC DDR WORLD|DanceDanceRevolution WORLD]] onwards, it is available by default for all players.
* AFRONOVA received CHALLENGE charts in [[CS DDR GRAND PRIX|DanceDanceRevolution GRAND PRIX]]'s GRAND PRIX mode on December 25th, 2025, which become available by purchasing '''GRAND PRIX chart pack vol.6''' (グランプリ譜面パック vol.6).
** By purchasing the pack with an active subscription, AFRONOVA's CHALLENGE charts can be played in DanceDanceRevolution WORLD.
** From December 28th, 2026 in DanceDanceRevolution WORLD, they are available by default for all players.

== Song Production Information ==
=== DanceDanceRevolution 3rdMIX Official Website ===
==== NAOKI ====
The song is a combination of Afro music, jungle & drum'n'bass, and was designed to create an interesting chart arrangement that could be easily linked to the rhythmic traps. Actually, this song was originally created to be D.D.R.'s next [[PARANOiA]].

=== DanceDanceRevolution 3rdMIX Original Soundtrack ===
Untranslated.

=== NAOKI MAEDA ===
This song was created with Africa as its concept.<br>
The sound is created so that if you listen, you can see the eminent image of a vast landscape of the savanna.<br>
Consequently, I think this song is filled with originality.

== CS Information Data ==
=== [[CS DDRMAX2 NA|DDRMAX2 -DanceDanceRevolution-]] ===
