== Trivia ==
{{Gallery}}
* MAXX UNLIMITED is DDRMAX2's EXTRA STAGE. To access it, you must AA a HEAVY chart in the FINAL STAGE. Clearing MAXX UNLIMITED with a AA or higher lets you access [[Kakumei|革命]] as the ONE MORE EXTRA STAGE.
** It can also be unlocked by reaching level 30, or using an operator code to unlock it via 6th PASS.
** In the [[CS DDRMAX2 JP|CS]] [[CS DDRMAX2 NA|releases]] of DDRMAX2, CHALLENGE charts can also be used to play MAXX UNLIMITED on EXTRA STAGE.
** From [[AC DDR EXTREME|DanceDanceRevolution EXTREME]] onwards, MAXX UNLIMITED is playable by default.
* During the DDRMAX2 location tests, MAXX UNLIMITED's title was capitalized as '''MAXX unlimited'''.
* With 105 jumps, MAXX UNLIMITED's Single BASIC chart has the highest number of jumps for any Single BASIC chart in the DanceDanceRevolution series.
** It is also the first BASIC chart to have over 100 jumps.
* MAXX UNLIMITED received a Single BEGINNER chart in DanceDanceRevolution EXTREME.
* In [[CS DDR ULTRAMIX2|DanceDanceRevolution ULTRAMIX2]] and [[CS DS Unleashed2|Dancing Stage Unleashed2]], MAXX UNLIMITED's BPM is displayed as 150-320.
* MAXX UNLIMITED's Single DIFFICULT chart was slightly modified in [[AC DDR X|DanceDanceRevolution X]], fixing some note quantizations.
* MAXX UNLIMITED's Single EXPERT chart is retroactively the first chart to be rated Level 16 on the current 1-20 difficulty scale.
* '''MAXX UNLIMITED(X-Special)''' is one of the X-Special EXTRA STAGEs in DanceDanceRevolution X, which can be played from July 30th, 2009 by obtaining AA on a set of CHALLENGE-only songs before the FINAL STAGE.
** As of October 1st, 2009, MAXX UNLIMITED(X-Special) has been unlocked for normal play.
* From [[AC DDR X2|DanceDanceRevolution X2]] onwards, MAXX UNLIMITED(X-Special) appears in the DanceDanceRevolution X folder instead of the DDRMAX2 folder.
* MAXX UNLIMITED was one of the qualifying round songs in the [[KONAMI Arcade Championship|KONAMI Arcade Championship 2013]] for [[AC DDR 2013|DanceDanceRevolution (2013)]].
* From June 1st, 2017 in [[AC DDR A|DanceDanceRevolution A]] to [[AC DDR A3|DanceDanceRevolution A3]], MAXX UNLIMITED(X-Special) does not appear in the song selection screen if the player does not use an [[e-amusement]] pass.
** From [[AC DDR WORLD|DanceDanceRevolution WORLD]] onwards, it is available by default for all players.

== Song Production Information ==
=== NAOKI ===
Positioned as DDR MAX2's most difficult song, it's an upper techno song unique to this game, with the BPM going up to 320, the fastest in the series.

Honestly, until I became involved in music production of music games, it was impossible to create a BPM320 song as a dance music. Anyways, those who can dance to a BPM320 song with an unprecedented dance style, to summarize in one word, are amazing.

