== Trivia ==
{{Gallery}}
* The "SP" in SP-TRIP MACHINE～JUNGLE MIX～'s title stands for "SPECIAL".
* SP-TRIP MACHINE～JUNGLE MIX～'s EXPERT charts have a step pattern that was later known by the fans as the "[[AFRONOVA]] walk", which is a long crossover section where the fourth note of the pattern starts another crossover, but is still an 8th note, instead of a 4th note.
** Despite its presence in SP-TRIP MACHINE～JUNGLE MIX～, the pattern became popular with AFRONOVA as it was used more prominently on its EXPERT charts.
* An unused Double MANIAC chart for SP-TRIP MACHINE～JUNGLE MIX～ can be found in the DanceDanceRevolution 2ndMIX data.
* According to dj TAKA's comments for SP-TRIP MACHINE(for beatmania II), SP-TRIP MACHINE～JUNGLE MIX～ was supposed to be appear in beatmania IIDX 2nd style. However, since all he got were the voice clips from the song from DE-SIRE, he had to re-arrange the song for beatmania IIDX personally.
* SP-TRIP MACHINE～JUNGLE MIX～ received a brand-new Double MANIAC chart in [[AC DDR 4th|DanceDanceRevolution 4thMIX]].
* From [[AC DDR EXTREME|DanceDanceRevolution EXTREME]] to [[AC DDR SuperNOVA2|DanceDanceRevolution SuperNOVA2]], SP-TRIP MACHINE～JUNGLE MIX～'s title was '''SP-TRIP MACHINE (JUNGLE MIX)'''.
* SP-TRIP MACHINE～JUNGLE MIX～ received a Single BEGINNER chart in DanceDanceRevolution EXTREME.
* SP-TRIP MACHINE～JUNGLE MIX～ received a Double BEGINNER chart in [[CS DDR ULTRAMIX3|DanceDanceRevolution ULTRAMIX3]].
** In DanceDanceRevolution ULTRAMIX3 and [[CS DS Unleashed3|Dancing Stage Unleashed3]], SP-TRIP MACHINE～JUNGLE MIX～'s title and artist were capitalized as '''SP - Trip Machine Jungle Mix''' and '''De-Sire''', respectively.
* '''SP-TRIP MACHINE～JUNGLE MIX～(X-Special)''' is one of the X-Special EXTRA STAGEs in [[AC DDR X|DanceDanceRevolution X]], which can be played from April 16th, 2009 by obtaining a AA or better on [[PARANOiA MAX~DIRTY MIX~|PARANOiA MAX～DIRTY MIX～]] as the FINAL STAGE. However, PARANOiA MAX～DIRTY MIX～ must be chosen by the RANDOM option.
** As of October 1st, 2009, SP-TRIP MACHINE～JUNGLE MIX～(X-Special) has been unlocked for normal play.
* From [[AC DDR X2|DanceDanceRevolution X2]] onwards, SP-TRIP MACHINE～JUNGLE MIX～(X-Special) appears in the DanceDanceRevolution X folder instead of the 2ndMIX folder.
* SP-TRIP MACHINE～JUNGLE MIX～ received SMM-Special charts in the [[CS DDR X JP|Japanese release of DanceDanceRevolution X CS]]. Instead of the BPM changes of PARANOiA MAX～DIRTY MIX～(SMM-Special), SP-TRIP MACHINE～JUNGLE MIX～(SMM-Special)'s charts are filled with stops.
** SP-TRIP MACHINE～JUNGLE MIX～(SMM-Special)'s BASIC chart can only be played in Street Master Mode.
** SP-TRIP MACHINE～JUNGLE MIX～(SMM-Special) has the most stops of ''any'' DanceDanceRevolution song to date, with 71 of them.
* In DanceDanceRevolution GB, SP-TRIP MACHINE～JUNGLE MIX～ runs at 161 BPM.
* From June 1st, 2017 in [[AC DDR A|DanceDanceRevolution A]] to [[AC DDR A3|DanceDanceRevolution A3]], SP-TRIP MACHINE～JUNGLE MIX～(X-Special) does not appear in the song selection screen if the player does not use an [[e-amusement]] pass.
** From [[AC DDR WORLD|DanceDanceRevolution WORLD]] onwards, it is available by default for all players.

