Experience high-energy dance that will keep you coming back for more.

== Song Production Information ==
=== beatmania IIDX ===
==== NAOKI ====
This song is an upper number from D.D.R.4th MIX, completely filled with NAOKI's sound, and the driving feeling of AARON G's MC, while the sharp synth leads and hit sounds combine with the beat like an addictive sensation, further enhancing its rave feeling.<br>
It's quite challenging in the game with the key placement in the first-half, and the intermittent scratching in the second half. By all means, I'd like you to create your own upper groove!!

=== DanceDanceRevolution 4thMIX Official Website ===
==== NAOKI MAEDA ====
B4U is a new song which I diligently created as an attempt to do what I couldn't do during the production of "BRILLIANT 2U", which was first included in D.D.R.2nd MIX, by using the current technology and technological capabilities to enhance it in every respect.<br>
To every player, by all means, please JUMP, JUMP, JUMP, DDR~~!! Please enjoy this B4U and play alongside the MC until dawn!

=== DanceDanceRevolution 4thMIX Original Soundtrack ===
==== NAOKI MAEDA ====
B4U's official name is BRILLIANT 4U, and it's the sequel to BRILLIANT 2U as its name suggests, which I finished in an entirely new form by powering it up in every aspect while retaining the same atmosphere.

==== Liner Notes ====
This is an authentic dance tune which D.D.R. freaks can't get enough of, with a deceptive speedy feeling from the very beginning. When the machine gun-like aggressive rap changes to the dazzling chorus sound, its tension should've reached its climax. Don't the occasional "D.D.R.!" shouts remind you of the highly popular and proud masterpiece "BRILLIANT 2U" from 2ndMIX?

=== [[CS DDR Party Collection|DanceDanceRevolution Party Collection]] ===
This number continues the flow from "BRILLIANT 2U", which is extremely popular among D.D.R. fans. The MC's energetic rap from the very beginning and the high-speed synths are the golden combination of Eurobeat. This authentic dance tune seems to capture the excitement of the dancefloor.

=== Dance Maniax ===
This number continues from "BRILLIANT 2U", which received overwhelming support throughout the D.D.R. series. It's included in D.D.R. 4thMIX, so perhaps many players have already heard it. The MC's energetic rap from the very beginning and the high-speed synths are the golden combination of Eurobeat. The gorgeous and danceable result seems to capture the excitement of the dancefloor. If you want to vigorously dance without thinking, please choose this number!

== CS Information Data ==
=== [[CS DDR EXTREME NA|DanceDanceRevolution EXTREME CS (North America)]] ===
You have unlocked the song "B4U" by NAOKI. Debuting on [[CS DDR KONAMIX|Dance Dance Revolution KONAMIX]], "B4U" is a perfect example of the ideal Dance Dance Revolution song with its physically challenging dance steps, fast-paced rhythms and vocals and competitive themes. Check out the new "B4 ZA BEAT MIX" in this game as well.

== Video Production Information ==
=== VJ GYO ===
The characteristic intro announces the start of "something" with a continuous high tension from "that song"!<br>
When [[AC substream|substream]]/[[AC DDR CLUB VER.2|CLUB VERSION 2]] were being produced at that time, all the team members participated in intense Battle play (during difficulty review/bug checks/trial playthrough), and it was well received in the market, who showed visible excitement and stood out.

However, I think you can recognize the true charm of B4U if you listen closely, which is a super power-up from "that song", which is "Brilliant 2U".<br>
It's full of speed and power which seems categorically more associated with "running" than "dancing", and defies the definition of a new flow of Euro high tension. The song is sublimated into a dimension, which reproduces the uplifting and euphoric feelings of a fighting spirit similar to a "battle"!

The route of NAOKI's upper Euro "car-themed" movie was discussed in a conversation with [[Takayuki Ishikawa|dj TAKA]] to be "quite on point". The well-known Mika Tsukuba appears as a rival in the movie!? (See the [https://web.archive.org/web/20150507123412fw_/http://www.konami.jp/am/bm2dx/bm2dx4/4th_question.html Q&A] section for details). With that scenario in mind, I created an original movie about car battles.<br>
The effect of having two characters appear was demonstrated in the chorus although it wasn't part of the story, which I think ended up becoming quite good.

Speaking of a battle between girls, dj TAKA and [[Keina Kanisawa|KANI]] witnessed a high score attack battle between two girls at an arcade when the production of IIDX 4th concluded, and I remember them filled with emotion and excitement as they said that "IIDX has entered a new phase～!".

