* A Eurobeat remix of BRILLIANT 2U by [[Youhei Hiroshige|DJ Command]], titled [[BRILLIANT 2U (AKBK MIX)]], appears in the 2011 re-release of the DanceDanceRevolution 2ndMIX ORIGINAL SOUNDTRACK album.
** A cut of this remix later appeared in [[AC DDR X3|DanceDanceRevolution X3 VS 2ndMIX]].
* A remix of BRILLIANT 2U appears as the Stage 1 theme in the PlayStation Portable port of ''Jikkyou Oshaberi Parodius'' (実況おしゃべりパロディウス). This replaces the original song used ([[That's The Way (I Like It)]]) in the Super Famicom/PlayStation/Saturn versions due to licensing issues.
* A shorter version of BRILLIANT 2U appears in the KONAMI arcade game ''Step Champ'' (ステップチャンプ) and the PlayStation game ''Bishi Bashi Special 3 ~Step Champ~'' (ビシバシスペシャル3 〜ステップチャンプ〜).
* BRILLIANT 2U's vocal samples originate from ''Heey Hoo AD'', a vocal track found on the sample CD ''RAPsody'' by Masterbits. 
** It shares these vocal samples with [[THE DEEP STRIKER]], from [[AC DJ TROOPERS|beatmania IIDX 15 DJ TROOPERS]].

== Trivia ==
{{Gallery}}
* BRILLIANT 2U is one of [[Noria Shiraishi]]'s favorite DanceDanceRevolution songs [https://web.archive.org/web/20070527110608/http://www.konami.jp/am/AM/DDR_ad/v_report4.html].
* BRILLIANT 2U was featured on the CM for the ''Toyota Celica'' car [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I2-hwM35jLA&feature=youtu.be].
* BRILLIANT 2U's beatmania IIDX video appears as a bonus movie in the [[beatmania IIDX VISUAL EMOTIONS 9]] DVD, where it was confirmed that VJ GYO made it.
* BRILLIANT 2U received LIGHT charts in [[AC 3rd style|beatmania IIDX 3rd style]].
* BRILLIANT 2U's background appears in [[five fathoms (beatmania II special version)]]'s video.
* An unused banner for BRILLIANT 2U can be found in the DanceDanceRevolution Best of Cool Dancers and [[AC DDR CLUB VER.1|DanceDanceRevolution 2ndMIX with beatmania IIDX CLUB VERSiON]] data. In this banner, BRILLIANT 2U is credited to '''VULGAR Inc.'''.
** An incomplete background can be found in the DanceDanceRevolution Best of Cool Dancers data as well.
*** Another unused background can be found in the 2ndMIX data. This unused background is taken from a background animation from the first [[AC DDR 1st|DanceDanceRevolution]] title.
* BRILLIANT 2U received a BEGINNER chart in [[AC DDR USA|DanceDanceRevolution USA]].
** It received a different BEGINNER chart in [[CS DDR BEST HITS|DanceDanceRevolution BEST HITS]], which is also used in [[CS DS EuroMIX|Dancing Stage EuroMIX CS]] and [[CS DDR NA|DanceDanceRevolution CS (North America)]].
** It received another different BEGINNER chart in [[AC DDR EXTREME|DanceDanceRevolution EXTREME]].
* In DanceDanceRevolution GB, BRILLIANT 2U plays at 145 BPM.
* BRILLIANT 2U received a new Single MANIAC chart in [[AC DDR 4th PLUS|DanceDanceRevolution 4thMIX PLUS]], replacing the old one.
** While this was reverted in [[AC DDRMAX2|DDRMAX2]], the 4thMIX PLUS MANIAC chart was still being used during the game's location tests.
** The 4thMIX PLUS MANIAC chart would later be added as a Single CHALLENGE chart in DanceDanceRevolution EXTREME, alongside a brand new Double CHALLENGE chart that features Freeze arrows.
* BRILLIANT 2U received a new unique video in [[CS DDR EXTREME2|DanceDanceRevolution EXTREME2]]. This video was carried to the arcade releases in [[AC DDR SuperNOVA|DanceDanceRevolution SuperNOVA]], and eliminates any on-screen dancers prior to [[AC DDR WORLD|DanceDanceRevolution WORLD]].
** A video based on its 2ndMIX animations is shown when BRILLIANT 2U is played from the [[DDR SELECTION]] folder.
* '''BRILLIANT 2U("STREAM" Special)''' is one of the My GROOVE RADAR (Myグルーヴレーダー) unlockable songs in [[AC DDR SuperNOVA2|DanceDanceRevolution SuperNOVA2]]. To unlock it, you must play songs that have charts which focus on the STREAM parameter of the [[GROOVE RADAR]].
** As of April 10th, 2008, BRILLIANT 2U("STREAM" Special) has been unlocked for normal play.
* Prior to [[AC DDR X2|DanceDanceRevolution X2]], BRILLIANT 2U ("STREAM" Special) had no space between its title and subtitle.
* BRILLIANT 2U is unlockable in [[CS INFINITAS|beatmania IIDX INFINITAS]] from December 8th, 2016, after purchasing its charts with [[CS INFINITAS/BIT unlocks|BITs]].
* From June 1st, 2017 in [[AC DDR A|DanceDanceRevolution A]] to [[AC DDR A3|DanceDanceRevolution A3]], BRILLIANT 2U ("STREAM" Special) does not appear in the song selection screen if the player does not use an [[e-amusement]] pass.
** From DanceDanceRevolution WORLD onwards, it is available by default for all players.
* In [[CS DDR GRAND PRIX|DanceDanceRevolution GRAND PRIX]], BRILLIANT 2U received its difficulty change from DanceDanceRevolution WORLD on July 3rd, 2024.

== Song Production Information ==
=== beatmania ===
==== NAOKI ====
The very fact that this song is in beatmania THE FINAL made me feel some sort of closure.<br>
Back when I was creating BRILLIANT 2U, [[AC bm 2nd|beatmania 2ndMIX]] had taken arcades by storm.<br>
How many years have passed since then?<br>
Times have changed, and the things that changed have changed significantly.<br>
As all of these things are starting to change, is there anything that stays the same?<br>
And just like the ebbs and flows of time, everything that has a beginning has an ending.<br>
Are the things we're doing now working to create a tomorrow after they've ended?<br>
It's a sad thing to only be able to remember the past.<br>
And that's why the future that continues beyond the end of beatmania... begins here.

=== DanceDanceRevolution 2ndMIX Official Website ===
==== NAOKI ====
I kind of like the sound of the word "brilliant", and the appearance of two people dancing is brilliant! I created this song with the concept of "let's go~ with a Euro royal road" in mind.

=== DanceDanceRevolution 2ndMIX Original Soundtrack ===
This is a KONAMI original song that appeared in 2nd MIX. It's a speedy dance number, reminiscent of works produced by production group Stock Aitken Waterman, who swept the world in the mid 1980s. Basic 4-bar bass drums, sharp brass sounds, increasing electric piano-like sound phrases, and hidden distortion guitars create a brilliant stereo space. Don't miss the groovy male rap as well. A special version is included in DISC-2.

=== DanceDanceRevolution 2ndReMIX APPEND CLUB VERSiON vol.2 ===
This is a song that represents DanceDanceRevolusion, which made KONAMI artist Naoki Maeda famous. It's included here with the feeling of playing it in Beatmania.<br>
Although the difficulty level is quite high when playing it in IIDX, if you're a DanceDanceRevolusion fan, you should try to play it in IIDX at least once.

=== [[CS DDR Party Collection|DanceDanceRevolution Party Collection]] ===
Ever since its first appearance in D.D.R. 2ndMIX, "BRILLIANT 2U" has created countless fans. Countless players turned into repeat players from the completely danceable hyper Euro sound. You can't talk about D.D.R. without listening to this masterpiece!

== CS Information Data ==
=== DanceDanceRevolution EXTREME2 ===
Debuting on [[CS DDR NA|DanceDanceRevolution]], "BRILLIANT 2U" is a classic from the series.<br>
Not only is NAOKI responsible for composing most of the KONAMI original music in the DanceDanceRevolution series, but songs like "BRILLIANT 2U" are considered theme songs of the game.<br>
Be sure to check out the new challenge level steps of the song as well as the new "K.O.G G3 MIX" in this game as well.

