== Lyrics ==
None.

== Song Connections / Remixes ==
* According to Naoki, DEAD END was originally going to be 260 BPM, and the song was named as such because of its speed. While it was reduced to 190 BPM due to "various reasons", Naoki would later release a song with 260 BPM, [[DROP OUT]], stating that both songs are "closely related" [https://peing.net/ja/q/02753177-e270-4557-8c2d-1bd3c17fd15b].
* A remix of DEAD END by B4 ZA BEAT appears in the [[DanceDanceRevolution 3rdMIX ORIGINAL SOUNDTRACK]] NONSTOP MEGAMIX.
* DEAD END is included in the song medley [[Non Stop Mix Special 2]] in [[AC DMX 2nd|Dance Maniax 2ndMIX]].
* DEAD END appears as part of the medley [[Aggro Mix]], from [[CS DDR UNIVERSE2|DanceDanceRevolution UNIVERSE2]].
* DEAD END shares the "revolution" vocal sample with [[AC DDR 1st|DanceDanceRevolution]]'s intro screen, [[DDR MEGAMIX]], [[New Millennium]], and [[Hou|鳳]].

== Trivia ==
{{Gallery}}
* DEAD END appears on the movies ''La máquina de bailar'' and ''Grandma's Boy''.
* DEAD END received a Single BEGINNER chart in [[AC DS EuroMIX|Dancing Stage EuroMIX]].
* DEAD END received new graphics in DanceDanceRevolution UNIVERSE2.
** Its title was also capitalized as '''Dead End'''.
* '''DEAD END("GROOVE RADAR" Special)''' is one of the My GROOVE RADAR (Myグルーヴレーダー) unlockable songs in [[AC DDR SuperNOVA2|DanceDanceRevolution SuperNOVA2]]. To unlock it, you must play songs to fill ''every'' parameter of the [[GROOVE RADAR]].
** As of April 10th, 2008, DEAD END("GROOVE RADAR" Special) has been unlocked for normal play.
* Unlike the original DEAD END's charts, DEAD END ("GROOVE RADAR" Special)'s BPM is 95-380, being the only My GROOVE RADAR unlock with different BPM values than its original charts.
** DEAD END ("GROOVE RADAR" Special)'s BPM changes are as follows:
<pre>95&rarr;(stop)&rarr;190&rarr;95&rarr;(stop)&rarr;95&rarr;(stop)&rarr;190&rarr;(stop)&rarr;95&rarr;380&rarr;190</pre>
* DEAD END ("GROOVE RADAR" Special) has a dummy Single BEGINNER chart, possibly used to sync the chart to the audio.
* DEAD END has never appeared on an non-Japanese PlayStation 2 release of DanceDanceRevolution.
** However, DEAD END("GROOVE RADAR" Special) appeared in [[CS DDR X2|DanceDanceRevolution X2 CS]] as a boss song.
* DEAD END's Single EXPERT chart was slightly modified in [[AC DDR X|DanceDanceRevolution X]], by changing the quantizations of the notes from measures 33 to 34.
* Prior to [[AC DDR X2|DanceDanceRevolution X2]], the artist for DEAD END and its "GROOVE RADAR" Special charts was displayed as '''N&S'''.
** Also prior to X2, DEAD END ("GROOVE RADAR" Special) had no space between its title and subtitle.
* From June 1st, 2017 in [[AC DDR A|DanceDanceRevolution A]] to [[AC DDR A3|DanceDanceRevolution A3]], DEAD END ("GROOVE RADAR" Special) does not appear in the song selection screen if the player does not use an [[e-amusement]] pass.
** From [[AC DDR WORLD|DanceDanceRevolution WORLD]] onwards, it is available by default for all players.

