* Brazilian Anthem marks TOMOSUKE's first use of his Berimbau '66 alias in GuitarFreaks & DrumMania.
** It also marks vocalist Geila Zilkha's debut in GuitarFreaks & DrumMania.
* According to TOMOSUKE, he had in mind to do a song like Brazilian Anthem back in [[AC DM2|drummania 2ndMIX]], but he went with [[MONDO STREET]] instead.
* Brazilian Anthem's GuitarFreaks & DrumMania charts were created by TOMOSUKE himself [https://mond.how/ja/topics/2xyfcbncwcat294].
* Brazilian Anthem received a Bass ADVANCED chart in [[AC GF7DM6|GUITARFREAKS 7thMIX]].
** This chart was slightly modified in [[AC GF10DM9|GUITARFREAKS 10thMIX]].
* Brazilian Anthem is available in GUITARFREAKS 10thMIX & drummania 9thMIX and [[AC GF11DM10|GUITARFREAKS 11thMIX & drummania 10thMIX]] with an e-AMUSEMENT account.
** Brazilian Anthem has been made automatically available in Standard Mode as of [[AC GFDM V|GuitarFreaks V & DrumMania V]].
* Brazilian Anthem's Bass BASIC chart was slightly modified in GuitarFreaks V.
* Brazilian Anthem's artist was capitalized as '''BERIMBAU '66''' in DanceDanceRevolution ULTRAMIX3.
* Brazilian Anthem received new charts in DanceDanceRevolution SuperNOVA.
** The song's original Double BEGINNER chart can still be found unused in the game's data.
* Brazilian Anthem received a new banner, with a different artist font, in [[CS DDR SuperNOVA JP|DanceDanceRevolution SuperNOVA CS (Japan)]]. This new banner was also used in [[CS DS SuperNOVA|Dancing Stage SuperNOVA CS]], and was shortly afterwards carried over to the arcade releases in [[AC DDR SuperNOVA2|DanceDanceRevolution SuperNOVA2]].
* Unlike most other songs, Brazilian Anthem's DanceDanceRevolution jacket is based on the song's banner instead of its original background artwork.
* Brazilian Anthem is available for play in GuitarFreaksXG & DrumManiaXG as an unlockable song in JukeBox #2 (June 9th, 2010).
** As of August 13th, 2010, it has been automatically unlocked into Standard Mode.
* Brazilian Anthem was one of 30 possible picks for songs for [[AC RB groovin'!! Upper|REFLEC BEAT groovin'!! Upper]]'s 7th Set (Users' SELECTION) of the BEMANI MUSIC FOCUS unlocking system.
* Brazilian Anthem could be unlocked in REFLEC BEAT 悠久のリフレシア from April 27th, 2017, as part of the ''HAPPY☆PARADISE campaign'' (HAPPY☆PARADISEキャンペーン).
** It received a slightly modified GuitarFreaks & DrumMania jacket on the REFLEC BEAT series.
** Since July 20th, 2017, it is available by default.
* Brazilian Anthem also appears in ''FORTUNE TRINITY'', a KONAMI medal redemption game.
** It also appears on KONAMI's VR rhythm game ''BEAT ARENA''.

