== Trivia ==
{{Gallery}}
* cachaca's title is a misspelling of cachaça, which is a type of distilled alcoholic beverage from Brazil.
* cachaca is available for play in GuitarFreaksXG & DrumManiaXG as an unlockable song in JukeBox #2 (June 9th, 2010).
** As of August 13th, 2010, it has been automatically unlocked into Standard Mode.
* cachaca has never been on a CS release of the original GuitarFreaks & DrumMania series.
* cachaca does not appear in the nonstop megamix of the [[DanceDanceRevolution SuperNOVA ORIGINAL SOUNDTRACK]] album.
* cachaca's title in [[CS DDR UNIVERSE|DanceDanceRevolution UNIVERSE]] is capitalized as '''Cachaca'''.
* cachaca received new graphics and a Double BEGINNER chart in DanceDanceRevolution UNIVERSE.
** Curiously, this Double BEGINNER chart can be found unused in the DanceDanceRevolution SuperNOVA data.
* cachaca is available in [[CS GD Konasute|コナステ GITADORA]] by purchasing '''Konasute GITADORA HISTORY PACK vol.4''' (コナステ GITADORA HISTORYパック vol.4).
* In [[CS DDR GRAND PRIX|DanceDanceRevolution GRAND PRIX]], cachaca received its difficulty change from [[AC DDR WORLD|DanceDanceRevolution WORLD]] on July 3rd, 2024.

== Song Production Information ==
=== Yoshihiko Koezuka ===
This song was made with the concept of "playing" different from the ordinary drum.<br>
I wonder if there's something interesting to tap this melody? ..Uh. So, I came up with a steel drum.<br>
All right, I'll shape a funny song! So I thought to try to put a chorus with a noisy feeling together with the samba-like music.<br>
The voice is Mokky-kun, along with the familiar Yah Yah's.<br>
Everyone, try to sing "♪la-la-lalalala~♪" in the second half.

