== Song Connections / Remixes ==
* JET WORLD is a rearranged, extended version of one of the music tracks from KONAMI's 1996 arcade basketball game ''SLAM DUNK 2'' (スラムダンク2, also known as ''RUN AND GUN 2''), which Mutsuhiko Izumi was the music composer of.
* JET WORLD shares several similarities with the John Mayall song ''[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zLp0AsKXMEs Room to Move]'', from his 1969 album, ''The Turning Point''.
* JET WORLD is the first song of Mutsuhiko Izumi's "JET" song series.
* A long version of JET WORLD appears in the [[GUITAR FREAKS 2nd MIX ORIGINAL SOUNDTRACK]] album. This version was made playable as '''JET WORLD (Long Version)''' in GUITARFREAKS 3rdMIX.
* JET WORLD appears as part of the song medley [[Non Stop Mix Special 1]], in [[AC DMX|Dance Maniax]]. 
* Part of JET WORLD is heard in the medley [[Jake in the Box]] in [[AC GFDM V4|GuitarFreaks V4 & DrumMania V4 RockxRock]].
* A remix of JET WORLD by [[Ryutaro Nakahara|Ryu☆]], titled [[JET WORLD (Ryu Remix)|JET WORLD (Ryu☆Remix)]], appears in the [[REFLEC BEAT groovin'!! Upper ORIGINAL SOUNDTRACK]] album.
** A short version of JET WORLD (Ryu☆Remix) appears in REFLEC BEAT groovin'!! Upper.

== Trivia ==
{{Gallery}}
* JET WORLD, [[Across the nightmare]], [[Depend on me]], and [[Waza]] are the only four songs to have been in every DrumMania arcade installment until [[AC GFDM V8|V8]].
* Despite that JET WORLD's BPM is displayed as 276 in the GuitarFreaks & DrumMania series, its charts actually run at 138 BPM. This also applies to JET WORLD (Long Version).
* JET WORLD's charts in the original GuitarFreaks series were created by [[Yuei Uematsu|Yuei]].
* According to [[Takehiro Nojiri|NOZZY]] in [[One Phrase Blues]]' video production information, the clown in JET WORLD's video is named ''Jet-kun'' (ジェット君).
** Jet-kun appears as a selectable character in [[AC GFDM V4|GuitarFreaks V4 & DrumMania V4 Яock×Rock]] and [[AC GFDM V7|GuitarFreaks & DrumMania V7]]'s BATTLE MODE.
* JET WORLD is one of the GUITARFREAKS 2ndMIX preview songs that appears in [[CS GF|GUITARFREAKS CS]]. To unlock it, complete 150 songs in ARCADE Mode.
* JET WORLD received a Drum BASIC chart in [[AC DM2|drummania 2ndMIX]].
* JET WORLD's EXPERT chart was removed in [[AC GF5DM4|GUITARFREAKS 5thMIX]]. The old EXTREME and EXTREME+ charts were moved down to the ADVANCED and EXTREME difficulties, respectively.
* JET WORLD (Long Version) received Drum charts in [[AC GF6DM5|drummania 5thMIX]].
* Unused graphical data for JET WORLD (Long Version) can be found in [[AC GF8DM7|GUITARFREAKS 8thMIX & drummania 7thMIX]].
* JET WORLD is the 14th song unlock of Sugoroku de 8 (すごろく de 8) in pop'n music 8. It can be unlocked from July 17th, 2002 through August 28th, 2002 by directly landing on the city Abashiri on your first trip around the board, or by passing it on your second trip around.
** JET WORLD's character rival, Mr.B.BONE, can be unlocked by directly landing on Abashiri on your fifth lap around the board, or by simply passing it on your sixth trip.
*** Mr.B.BONE was a former mascot of the GuitarFreaks series.
* Along with the other BEMANI songs crossed over to pop'n music 8, JET WORLD shows ♪♪♪♪♪ as the artist. This was never changed.
** JET WORLD's pop'n music charts were created by [[Tomoyuki Uchida|ucchie]].
* In beatmania / beatmania III, JET WORLD's title was capitalized as '''Jet World'''.
* JET WORLD's artist is romanized in the DanceDanceRevolution series to '''Mutsuhiko Izumi'''.
* In the beatmania and beatmania III series, JET WORLD's genre is '''GUITAR PUNK'''.
** In the ''DanceDanceRevolution EXTREME Limited Edition Music Sampler'' album, it is '''ROCK'N COUNTRY''' instead.
** In the beatmania IIDX series, JET WORLD's genre is shown in Japanese.
* JET WORLD was performed live at ''THE GITADO LIVE -BEMANI 10th Anniversary memorial event-'' concert in 2007.
** It was also performed at the ''BEMANI ROCK FES'16'' concert in 2016.
* To unlock JET WORLD in [[CS pnm 12|pop'n music 12 いろは CS]], you must have [[CS GFDM V|GuitarFreaks V & DrumMania V CS]] data on your PlayStation 2 memory card.
** If you don't have GuitarFreaks V & DrumMania V CS data, you must enter a code to temporarily unlock both Cassandra and JET WORLD.
* JET WORLD is available for play in GuitarFreaksXG & DrumManiaXG as an unlockable song in JukeBox #2 (June 9th, 2010).
** As of August 13th, 2010, it has been automatically unlocked into Standard Mode.
* JET WORLD was one of the songs available during the location test of the North American redemption game [[AC pnm POP'N|POP'N MUSIC]].
** It received a new jacket in POP'N MUSIC.
* JET WORLD could be unlocked in REFLEC BEAT groovin'!! Upper as part of the 4th Set (Ryu☆'s SELECTION) of the ''BEMANI MUSIC FOCUS'' unlocking system.
** From September 17th, 2015 onwards, it could be purchased from the REFLEC Shop for 3800 Refle.
** In [[AC RB VOLZZA|REFLEC BEAT VOLZZA]], it could be purchased in the Garage for 20 VOLZZA KEYs.
** In [[AC RB VOLZZA 2|REFLEC BEAT VOLZZA 2]], it was playable by default.
* After being removed from the initial release of [[AC RB Reflesia|REFLEC BEAT 悠久のリフレシア]], JET WORLD was revived on December 15th, 2016.
* JET WORLD is featured as a BGM in KONAMI's ''THE★BishiBashi'' arcade game.
* JET WORLD (CLASSIC) could be unlocked in [[AC GD EXCHAIN|GITADORA EXCHAIN]] as one of the ''GF&DM CHRONICLE'' 1999～2002 songs from March 7th, 2019, by playing two credits.
** In [[AC GD NEX+AGE|GITADORA NEX+AGE]], it could be unlocked from March 4th to June 21st, 2020 and from October 28th to November 29th, 2020 as part of the ''Thank you! GITADORA 21st kanshasai'' (サンキュー! ギタドラ21st感謝祭) event.
*** It could also be unlocked from July 8th to August 2nd, 2020 and from December 2nd, 2020 to January 3rd, 2021 as part of the ''GITADORA wo tomodachi to issho ni play shiyou!! Campaign'' (GITADORAを友達と一緒にプレーしよう!!キャンペーン).
** As of [[AC GD FUZZ-UP|GITADORA FUZZ-UP]], it is available by default.
* JET WORLD is available in beatmania IIDX INFINITAS (2020) by purchasing '''beatmania IIDX INFINITAS Music Pack vol.25''' (beatmania IIDX INFINITAS 楽曲パック vol.25).
* JET WORLD received a widescreen video in [[AC GD GALAXY WAVE DELTA|GITADORA GALAXY WAVE DELTA]]. This video consists of its original video tiled three times across the screen.
** This video is also used for its CLASSIC charts.
* JET WORLD received CHALLENGE charts in [[CS DDR GRAND PRIX|DanceDanceRevolution GRAND PRIX]]'s GRAND PRIX mode on August 28th, 2025, which become available by purchasing '''GRAND PRIX chart pack vol.3''' (グランプリ譜面パック vol.3).
** By purchasing the pack with an active subscription, JET WORLD's CHALLENGE charts can be played in [[AC DDR WORLD|DanceDanceRevolution WORLD]].
** From August 31st, 2026 in DanceDanceRevolution WORLD, they are available by default for all players.

