== Song Connections / Remixes ==
* 大見解 is the first song of Des-ROW's HIP ROCK song series.
* A long version of 大見解, titled ''大見解（長っ）'', appears in the [[pop'n music Vocal Best 3]] album. This version is the basis for '''大見解 (LONG)''' in pop'n music 9.
* The DanceDanceRevolution series uses a shorter version of 大見解, removing 4 measures from the intro.
* A different arrangement of 大見解 by Des-ROW・組スペシアルr, titled ''大見解コア'', appears in Des-ROW's first album, [[D.]].
* A remix of 大見解 by [[Takehiko Fujii|CALF]], titled [[Daikenkai no shinkenkai|大見解の新見解]], appears in [[AC pnm 16|pop'n music 16 PARTY♪]].
* 大見解 appears as part of the ''PM SUPER BEST すぺしゃるメドレー'', a medley by [[Tsugumi Kataoka]] that appears in the [[pop'n music SUPER BEST BOX]] compilation album.
* A cover of 大見解 by [[Reiji Sakurai]] was uploaded to his [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_wn1bc5owRI YouTube channel].

== Trivia ==
{{Gallery}}
* 大見解 marks ALPHA's debut in BEMANI.
** 大見解 being crossed over also marks their first appearance in the DanceDanceRevolution series.
*** Both 大見解 and [[BE LOVIN]] being crossed over also mark Osamu Migitera's first appearance in that series.
* "Roku" (六) is Japanese for "six".
** According to shio, his name was coined by pop'n music director [[Hajime Saito|saito]] (who also points the pun of "roku" with "rock").
* According to [[Chihiro Inoue|chihiro]]'s song comments for [[Daikenkai no shinkenkai|大見解の新見解]], she joined KONAMI shortly after 大見解 was completed.
* Before [[AC pnm 8|pop'n music 8]], in [[CS pnm 6|pop'n music 6 CS]], and in the DanceDanceRevolution series, 大見解's artist is shown as '''Des-ROW feat. TSUBOI for ALPHA'''.
** In the beatmania / beatmania III series, 大見解 is credited to '''Des-ROW'''.
* In beatmania THE FINAL, 大見解's BPM in the song selection screen is not displayed.
** In [[CS DDR ULTRAMIX3|DanceDanceRevolution ULTRAMIX3]] and [[CS DS Unleashed3|Dancing Stage Unleashed3]], its BPM is shown as 142-172.
* Unused songlist graphics for 大見解 appear in [[AC GF8DM7|GUITARFREAKS 8thMIX & drummania 7thMIX]], nine months before its first appearance in the GuitarFreaks & DrumMania series.
* 大見解 (LONG) is a hidden song in pop'n music 9. To unlock it; 
** Play any Des-ROW song for STAGE 1, with the number 6 appearing at least six times on score, max combo, GREATs, GOODs, and BADs.
** 大見解 (LONG) will then be playable on STAGE 2.
* 大見解 (LONG) received new HYPER and EX charts in the JAB revision of pop'n music 9.
* 大見解 (LONG) lost its subtitle in [[AC pnm 11|pop'n music 11]]. Since that game, it is simply known as '''大見解'''.
* In the DanceDanceRevolution series, 大見解 received a unique video (different from the GuitarFreaks & DrumMania video) in [[CS DDR EXTREME2|DanceDanceRevolution EXTREME2]]. This video was carried to the arcade releases in [[AC DDR SuperNOVA|DanceDanceRevolution SuperNOVA]], and eliminates any on-screen dancers prior to [[AC DDR WORLD|DanceDanceRevolution WORLD]].
** 六 appears in 大見解's DanceDanceRevolution video.
* In DanceDanceRevolution ULTRAMIX3, 大見解's title and artist were changed to '''Daikenkai''' and '''Des-ROW・UNION''', respectively.
** It also received a Double BEGINNER chart in DanceDanceRevolution ULTRAMIX3.
* 大見解 received a brand-new EX chart in pop'n music 16 PARTY♪. This chart uses a short version of HIP ROCK LONG (which was removed in the same pop'n music game).
** It received a different EX chart in [[CS pnm portable 2|pop'n music portable 2]]. This chart is exclusive to portable 2, and has never appeared in an arcade pop'n music title.
*** This chart uses the original 大見解 audio, instead of the one received in 16 PARTY♪.
** This version is also used for 大見解's ANOTHER charts in the beatmania IIDX series.
* 大見解 received an EASY chart in [[AC pnm Sunny Park|pop'n music Sunny Park]], replacing its old 5-Buttons chart.
* 大見解 is one of the songs featured on the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IZ5TWNGBqiA BEMANI SONGS ～Best of pop'n music～] video.
* 大見解 could be unlocked in REFLEC BEAT groovin'!! Upper as part of the 3rd Set (Des-ROW's SELECTION) of the ''BEMANI MUSIC FOCUS'' unlocking system.
** From September 17th, 2015 onwards, it could be purchased from the REFLEC Shop for 3800 Refle.
** In [[AC RB VOLZZA|REFLEC BEAT VOLZZA]], it could be purchased in the Garage for 20 VOLZZA KEYs.
** In [[AC RB VOLZZA 2|REFLEC BEAT VOLZZA 2]], it was playable by default.
* 大見解 received a new jacket in the REFLEC BEAT series, based on its GuitarFreaks & DrumMania video (however, it is different from its GuitarFreaks & DrumMania jacket).
* 大見解コア was performed at the ''BEMANI ROCK FES'16'' concert in 2016. 
* After being removed from the initial release of [[AC RB Reflesia|REFLEC BEAT 悠久のリフレシア]], 大見解 was revived on June 29th, 2017.
* 大見解 appears on KONAMI's mobile rhythm game ''ダンキラ!!! - Boys, be DANCING! -''.
* 大見解 is one of the BEMANI cassette tape songs hidden in ''METAL GEAR SURVIVE''.
** In ''METAL GEAR SURVIVE'', 大見解's title and artist were changed to '''DAIKENKAI''' and '''Des-ROW United''', respectively.
* 大見解 was released as a [[BEMANI Premium Archive Disc#Fourth Release|BEMANI Premium Archive Disc]] in November 2024.
* 大見解 is available in beatmania IIDX INFINITAS (2020) by purchasing '''beatmania IIDX INFINITAS Music Pack vol.27''' (beatmania IIDX INFINITAS 楽曲パック vol.27).

