* DXY! has never appeared on a PlayStation 2 DanceDanceRevolution release.
* DXY! is one of the few KONAMI originals in [[CS DDR ULTRAMIX|DanceDanceRevolution ULTRAMIX]] that does not appear in [[CS DS Unleashed|Dancing Stage Unleashed]].
* DXY! is available in [[CS INFINITAS|beatmania IIDX INFINITAS]] by purchasing '''beatmania IIDX INFINITAS Music Pack vol.5''' (beatmania IIDX INFINITAS 楽曲パック vol.5).

== Song Production Information ==
=== beatmania IIDX ===
==== dj TAKA ====
This is the most techno-styled techno song throughout the history of the beatmania series.<br>
The undulations of the synth sounds in this song are said to be unique to his live performances.<br>
Actually, when TaQ was stuck on an idea while arranging [[Voltage (feat. Hidemaru)|VOLTAGE]], he asked me "how does this sound?" while playing it on a synthesizer, and that sound eventually changed and appeared in DXY!.<br>
On the other hand, TaQ suggested to me "how about this hi-hat for this song?", which I used it in another song, so such mini collaborations seem to occur every day among close musicians.<br>
The origin of this song title was originally a parody of an onomatopoeia used in our inner-circle.<br>
"Hey! TaQ! Do you want to go there!!" It's a mystery if he tried to use it.

=== Dance Maniax ===
This is a minimal techno song with regular rhythms and a metallic touch. The crowded atmosphere created from completely removing the melody, provides listeners with a feeling of ecstasy. The repeated patterns from the opening suddenly changes its tone in the middle section, immediately raising the tension. Sounds that consume the mind are so addictive, that once you become addicted to them, they're unavoidable.

== Video Production Information ==
=== NEW-3 ===
This is an extremely cool song, and I was impatient but excited by it.<br>
I wanted to express its groove, texture, and development as comfortably as possible, so I integrated them with a common color.<br>
Also, although this was my first time using live-action materials, this video also taught me how interesting it was.

Off-topic, but when I later asked the composer TaQ to explain the meaning of "DXY!", he replied that it was "a substitute word for a greeting", but when I heard this song, I created the video with an image of a "killing machine" from beginning to end. Sorry (laughs).

== Staff Comments ==
These are comments by those involved in creating the background.

"During the initial stages, we went through a lot of trial and errors."

"When I got the OK sign, I was so happy that I first told my wife."

"Converting the sound wavelengths to the spectrum of light is completely... I'll think of something unreasonable."

"Sometimes I kept working at my desk, and before I knew it, it was the next morning."

"It was somehow my first attempt, so I was anxious about whether I could really complete it."

"It became a habit for me to shape my fingers like Fleming's law. It still won't untangle itself."

"I discovered a significant bug at the last minute, and the 174 hour all-nighter fix was hell."

"There were many ideas coming in, that it was difficult to gather them in one form."

"Just by listening 30 minutes every day, my English somehow improved. It feels like a dream."

"I went through a daze in 90 days."

"It was difficult, but I now feel like I've achieved something."

From their tireless efforts, the biggest project this century has safely been completed.

Sorry. I'm just kidding.

