== Trivia ==
{{Gallery}}
[[Image:Electro Tuned (the SubS mix) KONAMI.png|thumb|Measures 29 to 30 of Electro Tuned(the SubS mix)'s beatmania IIDX chart.]]
* "the SubS mix" is a reference to one of TaQ's closest friends from Germany, who goes by the name DJ SubSimon.
* According to an interview with TaQ, Electro Tuned(the SubS mix) was his first song produced for BEMANI [http://www.originalsoundversion.com/gdc-2010-from-beatmania-to-carnegie-hall-an-interview-with-taq/].
* Electro Tuned(the SubS mix)'s beatmania IIDX charts were created by TaQ himself.
** The notes at measures 29 to 30 of all of its charts (except BEGINNER) spell KONAMI (コナミ) in katakana.
* The sample at the beginning of Electro Tuned(the SubS mix) ("... some knocks, some disappointments, when sadness comes...") is from U.S. President Richard Nixon's farewell speech to the White House staff on August 9th, 1974.
* Electro Tuned(the SubS mix) received LIGHT charts in [[AC 3rd style|beatmania IIDX 3rd style]].
* An unused, slightly overwritten banner for Electro Tuned(the SubS mix) can be found in the DanceDanceRevolution 5thMIX data.
* Electro Tuned(the SubS mix)'s original background reuses the artwork of [[LIVIN' LA VIDA LOCA]], an unreleased license from [[AC DDR 4th PLUS|DanceDanceRevolution 4thMIX PLUS]].
* Electro Tuned(the SubS mix) received a BEGINNER chart and new graphics in [[AC DS EuroMIX2|Dancing Stage EuroMIX2]].
** It received a different banner in [[CS DDRMAX NA|DDRMAX -DanceDanceRevolution-]], based on the original background.
* Electro Tuned(the SubS mix)'s overlays were removed in [[AC 9th style|beatmania IIDX 9th style]].
** It received brand-new overlays in [[AC Pinky Crush|beatmania IIDX 32 Pinky Crush]].
* In the DanceDanceRevolution series, Electro Tuned(the SubS mix) was notable for containing an offsync measure. This was fixed in [[AC DDR X|DanceDanceRevolution X]], by shifting the notes at the beginning of the song a half beat earlier and removing a BPM change.
* From [[AC DDR X2|DanceDanceRevolution X2]] onwards, the DanceDanceRevolution series displays Electro Tuned(the SubS mix)'s title as '''Electro Tuned ( the SubS mix )'''.

== Song Production Information ==
=== [[Takayuki Ishikawa|dj TAKA]] ===
It's mid-tempo big beat.<br>
Throughout the song, it feels like a trance into the Arabian spiritual world.<br>
This song has a rather cool finish.<br>
If you're a IIDX techno fan, I'm sure you'll like it!<br>
What do you think of the note patterns in the middle of the song, which no one has ever thought of before!?

== CS Information Data ==
=== DDRMAX -DanceDanceRevolution- ===
You have unlocked the song "Electro Tuned(the SubS mix)" by TaQ. This song is packed with awesome breakbeat sounds straight from the underground dance scene.

== Video Production Information ==
=== VJ GYO ===
This song's movie is a generic video shared with new techno songs, but GOLI put a lot of pressure on me to make it look like something that would play at an actual club event, so I took on the challenge and made this ambitious work to take away my worries.<br>
The material was not designed to be controlled in real time by the player like a real VJ, nor were specifically done for any song or tempo, so we put some thought into how to take them and finish it in a distinctive fashion.<br>
Even the talented but harsh GOLI was convinced (he even created the typography and is a very nice person).<br>
I certainly think it was finished with a rather edgy image for an arcade game.

