* Prior to [[AC DDR WORLD|DanceDanceRevolution WORLD]], .59's BPM was shown as 135.

== Song Production Information ==
=== beatmania IIDX ===
==== dj TAKA ====
It seems like there's a lot of techno in games, so this ".59" is my answer.<br>
It's something that can be played in a IIDX game.<br>
It's rather difficult~.<br>
I wonder if I'm the only person on the staff that can clear it, huh.<br>
The history of German music, from Bach's Invention to German trance, is represented in this song!.<br>
The historic circumstances and occasional chaos of the East and West fusion are here too~ (lying).<br>
By the way, the entire staff was talking about the song's title.<br>
Its meaning..... VJ GYO will explain the answer!

=== DanceDanceRevolution ===
dj TAKA is known for composing [[GRADIUSIC CYBER]], which achieved tremendous popularity in [[AC 1st style|beatmania IIDX]] and [[AC DDR CLUB VER.2|D.D.R. CLUB VERSION]]. This song brilliantly fuses different genres, forming a distinct music world. The jazz part features a piano, the classical part with a magnificent worldview, and the techno sound gives it a cyber feel. You'll be strongly drawn to this great mysterious space which transcends genres.

== CS Information Data ==
=== [[CS DDR EXTREME NA|DanceDanceRevolution EXTREME (America)]] ===
".59" by dj TAKA debuted on [[CS DDR KONAMIX|Dance Dance Revolution KONAMIX]] and stands on its own as a really cool tech-house track. From the ambient influenced opening to the orchestral instruments to the driving house beat, ".59" will definitely get your house in the groove. Check out other songs by this artist in this game and Dance Dance Revolution KONAMIX, [[CS DDRMAX NA|DDRMAX Dance Dance Revolution]] and [[CS DDRMAX2 NA|DDRMAX2 Dance Dance Revolution]].

== Video Production Information ==
=== VJ GYO ===
Do you know how to pronounce ".59"?<br>
The correct answer is "Tengoku/Heaven", not "Period Fifty-nine".<br>
I ended up using a generic video for this movie, so GOLI tried his best in a limited time to come up with animations which appear when players press the keyboard.<br>
Since the song title doesn't say "tengoku" or "HEAVEN", the melody and animations simply don't associate with "heaven".<br>
Rather than praising those who reached their destination, I feel it contains a message of relief to those suffering along the way...

