== Song Connections / Remixes ==
* CELEBRATE NITE's rap originates from ''Female Rap 2'', a vocal track found on the sample CD ''RAPsody'' by Masterbits.
** Other segments of this track are used in [[LET THEM MOVE]], from [[AC DDR 2nd|DanceDanceRevolution 2ndMIX]], [[Small Waves]], from [[AC 4th style|beatmania IIDX 4th style]], and [[Try 2 Luv. U]], from [[CS DDRMAX2 NA|DDRMAX2 -DanceDanceRevolution-]].
* According to Naoki, CELEBRATE NITE is part of the [[BRILLIANT 2U]]&rarr;CELEBRATE NITE&rarr;[[DYNAMITE RAVE]] trilogy.
* Dancing Stage featuring TRUE KiSS DESTiNATiON's Super Maniac results BGM is based on CELEBRATE NITE.
* A portion of CELEBRATE NITE is included in [[NONSTOP G]] from DanceDanceRevolution Solo 2000.
* A remix of CELEBRATE NITE by B4 ZA BEAT appears in the [[DanceDanceRevolution Solo 2000 ORIGINAL SOUNDTRACK]] NONSTOP MEGAMIX.
* An 8-bit arrangement of CELEBRATE NITE appears in [[CS DDR GB3|DanceDanceRevolution GB3]].
* A trance remix of CELEBRATE NITE, titled [[CELEBRATE NITE(EURO TRANCE STYLE)]], appears in [[AC DDRMAX2|DDRMAX2 -DanceDanceRevolution 7thMIX-]]. 
* A remix of CELEBRATE NITE by [[William Shillito|DM Ashura]], titled [[CELEBRATE NITE Like It's '99 Mix]], appears in [[CS DDR ULTRAMIX4|DanceDanceRevolution ULTRAMIX4]].
* A cover of CELEBRATE NITE featuring new vocals by [[Angie Lee]], titled [[CELEBRATE NIGHT]], appears in [[CS DDR FuruFuruParty|ダンスダンスレボリューション フルフル♪パーティー]].

