== Song Connections / Remixes ==
* According to Naoki, DROP OUT is "closely related" to [[DEAD END]] from [[AC DDR 3rd|DanceDanceRevolution 3rdMIX]], song which was originally going to be 260 BPM [https://peing.net/ja/q/02753177-e270-4557-8c2d-1bd3c17fd15b].
* A remix of DROP OUT by K.O.G (KCP) appears in the [[DanceDanceRevolution Solo 2000 ORIGINAL SOUNDTRACK]] NONSTOP MEGAMIX. It was later included in [[AC DDRMAX2|DDRMAX2 -DanceDanceRevolution 7thMIX-]] under the title [[DROP OUT(FROM NONSTOP MEGAMIX)]].
* A portion of DROP OUT is included in [[NONSTOP I]] from DanceDanceRevolution Solo 2000.
* One of the sounds in DROP OUT can also be heard in [[Headache]] and [[Under Construction]]. 
* DROP OUT appears as part of the song medley [[Non Stop Mix Special 1]] in [[AC DMX|Dance Maniax]].

== Trivia ==
{{Gallery}}
* At the time of its release, DROP OUT held the record of the highest BPM in the DanceDanceRevolution series. It was later beaten by [[MAX 300]]'s 300 BPM in [[AC DDRMAX|DDRMAX -DanceDanceRevolution 6thMIX-]].
** Also, it held the record of the highest constant BPM in the DanceDanceRevolution series until [[Across the nightmare]] in [[AC DDR EXTREME|DanceDanceRevolution EXTREME]].
* DROP OUT was used as the background music in DanceDanceRevolution Solo 2000's scoreboard part of the demo loop. 
* DROP OUT received Double charts in DanceDanceRevolution 4thMIX.
* DROP OUT's background and charts can be found unused in the [[CS DDR 4thMIX|DanceDanceRevolution 4thMIX CS]] data.
* In [[CS DDR EXTRA MIX|DanceDanceRevolution EXTRA MIX]], DROP OUT reuses [[Holic]]'s background animations.
* DROP OUT has an additional chart in DanceDanceRevolution EXTRA MIX's CHALLENGE MODE, which is played on the first mission of the EXTRA course.
* DROP OUT received a Single BEGINNER chart in DanceDanceRevolution EXTREME.
* DROP OUT's EXPERT charts were slightly modified in [[AC DDR X|DanceDanceRevolution X]], rounding the 16th notes near the end of the song to 4th notes.
* DROP OUT appears as downloadable content for [[CS DDR S+|DanceDanceRevolution S+]], in the '''DDR 4thMIX Pack'''.
* DROP OUT received CHALLENGE charts in [[CS DDR GRAND PRIX|DanceDanceRevolution GRAND PRIX]]'s GRAND PRIX mode on July 11th, 2025, which become available by purchasing '''GRAND PRIX chart pack vol.2''' (グランプリ譜面パック vol.2).
** By purchasing the pack with an active subscription, DROP OUT's CHALLENGE charts can be played in [[AC DDR WORLD|DanceDanceRevolution WORLD]].
** From July 31st, 2026 in DanceDanceRevolution WORLD, they are available by default for all players.

