== Trivia ==
{{Gallery}}
* In the arcade beatmania titles from 3rd style to [[AC 6th style|6th style]], era (nostalmix)'s title was shown as '''era (Nostal mix)''' on its title card.
** In [[AC 7th style|7th style]] and [[AC 8th style|8th style]], it is capitalized as '''era (nostal mix)''' instead.
* At the time of its debut, era (nostalmix)'s Double ANOTHER chart had the most notes of any beatmania IIDX chart, with 1226 notes.
** This record was beaten [[AC 4th style|one game later]] by another TaQ song, [[DXY!]], whose Double ANOTHER chart contains 1529 notes.
** Its Double ANOTHER chart is one of the first charts to be (retroactively) rated Level 12 in either Single or Double Play mode, the other being [[Holic]], which debuted in the same game and also had its Double ANOTHER chart rated Level 12.
* Prior to [[AC 9th style|beatmania IIDX 9th style]], era (nostalmix)'s BPM was displayed as 89-179 in games from the beatmania III and IIDX series.
* In the beatmania III series, the title for era (nostalmix)'s ANOTHER charts changes to '''era (step mix)''', despite using era (step remix) for the audio.
* era (nostalmix) received a new BEGINNER chart in [[AC IIDX RED|beatmania IIDX 11 IIDX RED]].
** This chart was removed in [[AC GOLD|beatmania IIDX 14 GOLD]].
* era (nostalmix) received a Single BEGINNER chart in [[AC DS EuroMIX2|Dancing Stage EuroMIX2]].
* era (nostalmix) received a Double BEGINNER chart, as well as a different Single BEGINNER chart, in [[CS DDR ULTRAMIX2|DanceDanceRevolution ULTRAMIX2]].
** In the DanceDanceRevolution ULTRAMIX series, era (nostalmix) is titled as '''era nostalmix'''.
* era (nostalmix)'s Double DIFFICULT chart was slightly modified in [[AC DDR X|DanceDanceRevolution X]], fixing its minor quantization issues.
* Prior to [[AC Lincle|beatmania IIDX 19 Lincle]], era (nostalmix) is one of the few songs where its HYPER chart (12) is rated higher than the ANOTHER chart (11) in Double.
* era (nostalmix) could be unlocked in REFLEC BEAT groovin'!! Upper as part of the 1st Set ([[Yoshihiro Tagawa|DJ TOTTO]]'s SELECTION) of the ''BEMANI MUSIC FOCUS'' unlocking system, after unlocking the other songs of the 1st Set.
** Its SPECIAL chart could be unlocked via the BEMANI MUSIC FOCUS event as well after unlocking era (nostalmix)'s BASIC/MEDIUM/HARD charts.
*** era (step mix) is used for the SPECIAL/WHITE HARD chart's audio, with the title in the jacket changing accordingly. However, outside of the jacket, the song title in the game still remains "nostalmix".
** From September 17th, 2015 onwards, it could be purchased from the REFLEC Shop for 3800 and 1500 Refle for its BASIC/MEDIUM/HARD and SPECIAL charts, respectively.
** In [[AC RB VOLZZA|REFLEC BEAT VOLZZA]], its BASIC/MEDIUM/HARD charts could be purchased in the Garage for 20 VOLZZA KEYs. Its SPECIAL chart could be purchased for 8 VOLZZA KEYs after clearing the song.
** In [[AC RB VOLZZA 2|REFLEC BEAT VOLZZA 2]], it was playable by default.
** DJ TOTTO mentioned that era (nostalmix) is one of his musical roots.
* era (nostalmix) received a new jacket in the REFLEC BEAT series.
* era (nostalmix) marks TaQ's first appearance in the REFLEC BEAT series.
* era (nostalmix) is unlockable in [[CS INFINITAS|beatmania IIDX INFINITAS]] from October 5th, 2016, after purchasing its charts with [[CS INFINITAS/BIT unlocks|BITs]].
** From April 20th, 2022, it is available by default in [[CS INFINITAS 2020|beatmania IIDX INFINITAS (2020)]].
* After being removed from the initial release of [[AC RB Reflesia|REFLEC BEAT 悠久のリフレシア]], era (nostalmix) was revived on May 18th, 2017.
* era (nostalmix) also appears as one of the background music selectable to play during Accel Rave Time (アクセルレイブタイム) in ''SEVEN'S BEAT'' (セブンスビート), a KONAMI medal redemption game.

