== Song Connections / Remixes ==
* Holic is part of TaQ's "-ic" song series.
* A mix of Holic with [[stoic]] appears in TaQ's [[bounce connected]] album.

== Trivia ==
{{Gallery}}
* Holic contains three different time signatures in each section: 7/8 from the beginning, 7/4 during the middle, and 4/4 towards the ending.
* According to GOLI's comments in the [https://web.archive.org/web/20150507031218fw_/http://www.konami.jp/am/bm2dx/bm2dx4/4th_question.html Q&A corner] of the [[AC 4th style|beatmania IIDX 4th style]] official website, the character in Holic's overlays resembled a certain DJ who performed at a club he used to attend. 
* Holic is a hidden revival in [[AC DDRMAX2|DDRMAX2 -DanceDanceRevolution 7thMIX-]]. It can be unlocked by reaching level 13, or using an operator code to unlock it via 3rd PASS.
** From [[AC DDR EXTREME|DanceDanceRevolution EXTREME]] onwards, it is playable by default.
* Holic received a Single BEGINNER chart in [[AC DDR EXTREME|DanceDanceRevolution EXTREME]].
** A Single CHALLENGE chart for Holic can also be accessed in DanceDanceRevolution EXTREME via a glitch, though it is just a copy of its Single HEAVY chart.
* Holic is one of the first beatmania IIDX songs to have a Level 11 chart on Single retroactively, as the 1-12 rating scale wouldn't be introduced until [[AC HAPPY SKY|beatmania IIDX 12 HAPPY SKY]]. (The other song is [[R5]], which also debuted in beatmania IIDX 3rd style.)
** Holic and [[era (nostalmix)]] are the first songs with a Double chart rated Level 12.
* Holic's overlays were removed from the beatmania IIDX arcade games as of [[AC tricoro|beatmania IIDX 20 tricoro]] due to technical issues.
* Holic is unlockable in [[CS INFINITAS 2020|beatmania IIDX INFINITAS (2020)]] from June 7th, 2023 after purchasing its charts with [[CS INFINITAS/BIT unlocks|BITs]].
* Holic received CHALLENGE charts in [[AC DDR WORLD|DanceDanceRevolution WORLD]], unlockable from December 25th, 2024 through ''EXTRA SAVIOR WORLD''.

== Song Production Information ==
=== beatmania IIDX ===
==== [[Takayuki Ishikawa|dj TAKA]] ====
This is TaQ's Holic, a.k.a. "HARD TEC", his latest techno song.<br>
By the way, I received questions asking "how do you pronounce TaQ?", so the correct answer is "Taku".<br>
Q is pronounced "ku" in German, right? TaQ spent his childhood years in Germany, and it seems to be his favorite nickname since then.<br>
Many people also felt that TaQ's songs, such as Holic, have a certain German atmosphere to them, so perhaps it's from that background.

=== DanceDanceRevolution ===
This is a techno number by TaQ, who also created "era". The melody here is further removed, giving listeners a mechanical and aggressive impression. The gradually increasing tension creates an anxious feeling, while the subtle and profound synthesizer sounds make you feel a mysterious comfort. The last section immediately fades out from the continuous patterned phrases, leaving trailing notes like they're left behind.

== CS Information Data ==
=== [[CS DDRMAX NA|DDRMAX -DanceDanceRevolution-]] ===
You have unlocked the song "Holic" by TaQ. If you like the words "dark", "fast", and "hard techno", then you should also add the word "Holic" to your list.

== Video Production Information ==
=== VJ GYO ===
Both dj TAKA's "[[LEADING CYBER]]" and TaQ's "Holic" perfectly express the worldview of 3rd style's catchphrase, "CYBER beat NATION", in the most straightforward way.<br>
If anything, they're songs with dark tones and filled with power, like being consumed by an intense force, without sinking or stagnating.

